2026-04-01 21:20:51 [nitro@ryzen5] with geminit tool results in history have what role and content type?
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] In the context of the Gemini API and tool-use workflows, the interactions follow a specific
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] structure:
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1. Roles
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] The conversation history typically uses three roles to manage tool execution:
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] • `user`: Contains the initial prompt or request from the user.
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] • `model`: Contains the model's response. When the model decides to use a tool, this role
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] includes a `function_call` object specifying the tool name and arguments.
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] • `tool`: Contains the result of the tool execution. This role is used to feed the output
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] of the function back into the model so it can formulate a final answer.
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2. Content Structure
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] When a tool result is injected into the history, it is structured as follows:
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] • `role`: Must be set to `"tool"`.
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] • `parts`: An array containing a `function_response` object.
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   `name`: The name of the function that was executed (must match the `function_call`
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] name from the previous `model` turn).
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   `response`: An object containing the output of the function, typically structured
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] as `{"result": ...}` or a JSON representation of the data returned by the tool.
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] Example Sequence
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] [
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]   {"role": "user", "parts": [{"text": "What is the weather in Tokyo?"}]},
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]   {
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]     "role": "model",
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]     "parts": [{"function_call": {"name": "get_weather", "args": {"location": "Tokyo"}}}]
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]   },
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]   {
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]     "role": "tool",
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]     "parts": [{"function_response": {"name": "get_weather", "response": {"result": "Sunny, 25C"}}}]
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite]   }
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] ]
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:20:55 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:27 [nitro@ryzen5] oops, for some reason i have used role function when preparing history for a slopfountain gemini prompt
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] In your provided code, the use of `role: "function"` in `prepareGeminiPrompt` is technically
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] deprecated by the Google Generative AI SDK, though it might still be accepted by some older
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] or specific API endpoints.
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] Why this is happening
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] When Gemini is configured to use tools, the API expects a specific conversational flow. The
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] standard for the `tool` role in modern Gemini API implementations is:
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  Model: Sends a `function_call`.
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  User/Tool: Sends a `function_response` wrapped in a `tool` role.
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] In your `prepareGeminiPrompt` function:
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] case "tool":{
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite]     const response=textify(text);
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite]     const functionResponse={name:item.name,response};
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite]     if (debugging) echo("[GEMINI] functionResponse",functionResponse);
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite]     // You are currently using "function" as the role here:
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite]     contents.push({role:"function",parts:[{functionResponse}] });
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] The Fix
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] To align with the current Gemini API standards, you should change the role from `"function"` to
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] `"tool"`.
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Update your code to this:*
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] case "tool":{
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite]     const response=textify(text);
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite]     const functionResponse={name:item.name,response};
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite]     if (debugging) echo("[GEMINI] functionResponse",functionResponse);
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:33 [gemini-3.1-lite]     // Change role to "tool"
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite]     contents.push({role:"tool",parts:[{functionResponse}] });
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] Important Notes:
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Role Mapping: The Gemini API specifically looks for `role: "tool"` to identify that the
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] content contains the output of a previously requested function call.
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Part Structure: The `functionResponse` object inside the `parts` array is correct; only
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] the top-level `role` string needs to be updated.
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] • SDK Compatibility: If you are using the latest `npm:@google/generative-ai` package, using
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] `role: "function"` will likely trigger a validation error or be ignored, causing the model to lose
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] the context of the tool result. Using `role: "tool"` ensures the model correctly associates the
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] data with the previous `function_call`.
2026-04-01 21:24:34 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
