2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] Since you are using the official `@google/generative-ai` SDK in Deno, the SDK enforces a specific
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] schema for the `contents` array that differs slightly from the raw REST API.
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] When using the SDK's `generateContent` method, the `role` property is actually automatically
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] handled by the SDK based on the contents of the `parts` array.
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] The Problem
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] In the official SDK, you do not manually set `role: "tool"` or `role: "function"` as a
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] top-level property for the `contents` object. If you try to pass `{role: "tool", parts: [...]}` to
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] the SDK, it may throw a validation error because it expects a specific structure.
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] The Correct Approach
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] For the official SDK, the `contents` array should look like this:
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  For User messages: `{ role: "user", parts: [{ text: "..." }] }`
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  For Model messages: `{ role: "model", parts: [{ text: "..." }, { functionCall: {...} }]
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] }`
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3.  For Tool results: Use the `FunctionResponse` part type.
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Update your `prepareGeminiPrompt` logic to this:*
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] case "tool": {
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]     const response = textify(text);
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]     const functionResponse = {
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]         name: item.name,
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]         response: JSON.parse(response) // Ensure response is an object, not a string
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]     };
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]     if (debugging) echo("[GEMINI] functionResponse", functionResponse);
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]     // The SDK expects the part to be a functionResponse object
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]     contents.push({
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]         role: "function", // The SDK maps this internally
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]         parts: [{ functionResponse }]
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite]     });
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] Why it works this way:
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] • SDK Abstraction: The `GoogleGenerativeAI` SDK is a wrapper. When you pass `role:
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] "function"` to the SDK, it internally maps it to the correct API request format.
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] • `functionResponse`: The SDK specifically looks for the `functionResponse` key inside the
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] `parts` array to trigger the correct tool-use behavior.
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] • JSON requirement: Ensure the `response` field inside `functionResponse` is a
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] JavaScript object, not a stringified string. If your `textify` function returns a JSON
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] string, you must `JSON.parse()` it before passing it to the `functionResponse` object.
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Summary for your Deno/SDK setup:*
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] Keep the role as `"function"` (as the SDK expects this label to trigger the mapping), but ensure
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] the internal structure of the part is strictly `{ functionResponse: { name: string, response:
2026-04-01 21:27:22 [gemini-3.1-lite] object } }`.
