2026-04-03 04:06:00 [gemini-3.1-lite] The error occurs because the Google Gemini API (specifically the `FunctionResponse` part) expects
2026-04-03 04:06:00 [gemini-3.1-lite] the `response` field to be a JSON Object (Struct), but the code is passing a
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] JSON-serialized string.
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] In your `prepareGeminiPrompt` function (around line 720), you are calling `textify(text)` which
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] results in a string, and then putting that string into the `response` field.
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] The Fix
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] You need to ensure that the `response` field for a `functionResponse` is a plain JavaScript object,
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] not a stringified JSON.
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] Update the `tool` case within `prepareGeminiPrompt` (near line 720) as follows:
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] // Update this section in prepareGeminiPrompt
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] case "tool": {
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	// Ensure the content is parsed back into an object if it's a string
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	let responseObj;
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	try {
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		responseObj = typeof text === 'string' ? JSON.parse(text) : text;
2026-04-03 04:06:01 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	} catch (e) {
