2026-04-06 06:23:32 [nitro@ryzen5] summarise design in md format please
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] System Design Summary
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Core Architecture*
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Video Format: YPbPr (Component Video).
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Palette: 16-bit packed (4 bits Y, 3 bits Pb, 3 bits Pr + 6 bits padding/control).
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Timing: 148.5 MHz PIO clock (10 cycles per pixel).
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Sync Logic: `vidblit.pio` (SM0) handles horizontal/vertical timing and pedestal blanking.
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Data Pipeline: 4-channel DMA broadcast to 4 separate State Machines.
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Hardware Stages*
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  SM0 (Y-Pedestal): Tristate output for sync and black-level reference.
2026-04-06 06:23:36 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  SM1 (Y-Detail): 3-bit PDM grayscale modulation on top of Pedestal.
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3.  SM2/SM3 (Pb/Pr): 3-bit PDM color-difference modulation.
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] 4.  SM4 (Negative Rail): Dedicated charge pump driver (or AC coupling).
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] 5.  Attenuation: GPIO-switched resistors for "Half-Bright" mode.
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Resistor/Output Logic*
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Y-Output: Summing network (Pedestal + Detail) into 75Ω load.
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Chroma-Outputs: PDM signals mixed with negative rail (or AC-coupled) into 75Ω load.
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Half-Bright: Single or triple GPIOs switch reference resistors to ground to attenuate
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] active video levels without affecting sync timing.
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Data Flow*
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] • DMA: 4 channels (DREQ-paced) stream packed pixels to SM0-SM3.
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Bit-Stripping: SMs use `out null` instructions to isolate their specific bits from the
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] 16-bit word.
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] • PDM Generation: Expander SMs jump to 10-cycle patterns based on 3-bit pixel values.
2026-04-06 06:23:37 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:21 [nitro@ryzen5] am hoping to implement simple gif89 that cludges uncompressed pixel stream
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] To implement a "cludged" uncompressed GIF stream, you need to follow the LZW specification for a
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] clear code followed by literal data, but simplified. The key is that even in an "uncompressed"
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] stream, GIF requires data to be broken into sub-blocks (max 255 bytes) and terminated by a
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] zero-length block.
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] In your `BitPacker`, the logic is currently attempting to treat pixels as 5-bit codes. For a raw
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 4-bit pixel stream (using a 16-color palette), you should use a 4-bit code size.
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] Here is the corrected `BitPacker` and the modified `writeLzw` method.
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] Updated BitPacker
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] class BitPacker {
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	private buffer = 0;
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	private bitCount = 0;
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	private bytes: number[] = [];
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	// Use a fixed 4-bit code size for raw 16-color data
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	write(code: number): void {
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		this.buffer |= (code & 0x0F) << this.bitCount;
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		this.bitCount += 4;
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		while (this.bitCount >= 8) {
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 			this.bytes.push(this.buffer & 0xFF);
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 			this.buffer >>= 8;
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 			this.bitCount -= 8;
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		}
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	}
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	finish(): Uint8Array {
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		if (this.bitCount > 0) {
2026-04-06 11:39:28 [gemini-3.1-lite] 			this.bytes.push(this.buffer & 0xFF);
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		}
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		return new Uint8Array(this.bytes);
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	}
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] Updated writeLzw
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] In the GIF spec, the "Initial Code Size" is the number of bits needed to represent the palette
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] indices (4 bits for 16 colors). The stream must start with a `CLEAR` code (16).
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] private writeLzw(pixmap: Pixmap16): void {
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	const CLEAR = 16;
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	const EOI = 17;
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	const packer = new BitPacker();
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	packer.write(CLEAR);
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	for (let y = 0; y < pixmap.height; y++) {
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		for (let x = 0; x < pixmap.width; x++) {
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 			packer.write(pixmap.point4(x, y));
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		}
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	}
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	packer.write(EOI);
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	const data = packer.finish();
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	// 4 = LZW minimum code size (bits required for 16 colors)
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	this.file!.writeSync(new Uint8Array([4]));
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	let i = 0;
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	while (i < data.length) {
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		const chunkSize = Math.min(255, data.length - i);
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		this.file!.writeSync(new Uint8Array([chunkSize]));
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		this.file!.writeSync(data.subarray(i, i + chunkSize));
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		i += chunkSize;
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	}
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	this.file!.writeSync(new Uint8Array([0])); // Block terminator
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
