2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] Important Note on your `Pixmap16`
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] Your `Pixmap16` currently uses a `Uint32Array` to store four 4-bit pixels per 32-bit word
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] (`0x00000000`). If you are iterating `x` by 1 and calling `point4`, ensure your `point4` logic
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] correctly maps the bit-packed structure.
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] If you want to keep the implementation "cludgy" and simple, ensure that the `Initial Code Size`
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] byte (written before the sub-blocks) matches the bit-depth of your data (4 for 16 colors). Most
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] decoders will accept the stream if the code size is set correctly, even if the LZW dictionary isn't
2026-04-06 11:39:29 [gemini-3.1-lite] actually being built.
