2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] Standard GIF decoders are extremely sensitive to the very first few bytes of the LZW stream.
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1. The Bit-Width Correction
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] In the GIF spec, the "Initial Code Size" is 4. The first code sent must be `CLEAR` (16).
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] The decoder starts at `codeSize + 1` bits (which is 5). Your `LzwEncoder` is currently starting
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] with `bitWidth = 5`, which is correct, but your `BitPacker` logic needs to ensure it doesn't
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] accidentally truncate or shift incorrectly on the very first write.
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2. The Dictionary Reset Fix
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] When you reset the dictionary, you must immediately send a `CLEAR` code (16) at the
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] previous bit-width, and then the next code should be sent at the initial
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] bit-width (5).
2026-04-06 11:58:24 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
