2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3. The "Gotcha": Byte Alignment
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] If VS Code is still complaining, it is likely because your `BitPacker` leaves trailing bits in the
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] `buffer` after `EOI` is written.
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] Ensure that your `BitPacker.finish()` method does not leave a partial byte if you want to
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] be 100% compliant, though most decoders ignore it. However, if the `EOI` is not properly flushed,
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] some decoders (like those in Windows/VS Code) will report an "unexpected end of stream."
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Check your finish:*
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] finish(): Uint8Array {
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite]     // If there are bits left, write them as a final byte
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite]     if (this.bitCount > 0) {
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite]         this.bytes.push(this.buffer & 0xFF);
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite]     }
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite]     return new Uint8Array(this.bytes);
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] This is correct. If it still fails, the only remaining possibility is that your `Pixmap16.point4`
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] is returning values outside the 0-15 range, or your `palette` has fewer than 16 entries (your code
2026-04-06 11:58:25 [gemini-3.1-lite] has 16, which is correct). Double check that `pixmap.point4` never returns a value > 15.
