2026-04-06 12:06:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] accidentally sending a 16th color?*
2026-04-06 12:06:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] Check your `Pixmap16` bounds. If any pixel index is `16` or higher, the LZW encoder will break.
2026-04-06 12:06:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:06:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] If you are absolutely sure all pixel values are `0-15`, and `0xF3` works on Windows, then the file
2026-04-06 12:06:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] is technically perfect. VS Code's error is likely a false positive caused by the fact that you are
2026-04-06 12:06:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] "rolling your own" LZW rather than using a standard library, and the previewer is failing to follow
2026-04-06 12:06:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] your custom-built dictionary.
