2026-04-06 12:08:49 [gemini-3.1-lite] The Final Validation: The "Zero-Subblock"
2026-04-06 12:08:49 [gemini-3.1-lite] There is one more thing: The final block terminator.
2026-04-06 12:08:49 [gemini-3.1-lite] In your `writeLzw` method:
2026-04-06 12:08:49 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:08:49 [gemini-3.1-lite] this.file!.writeSync(new Uint8Array([0]));
2026-04-06 12:08:49 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:08:49 [gemini-3.1-lite] This is correct. However, some decoders are extremely sensitive to trailing bytes after
2026-04-06 12:08:49 [gemini-3.1-lite] this `0`. If your `Deno.FsFile` write operations are buffered, you might be writing the `0x3B` (GIF
2026-04-06 12:08:49 [gemini-3.1-lite] Trailer) immediately after the `0` block terminator without a clean flush.
