2026-04-06 12:11:39 [gemini-3.1-pro] compression compared to the more lenient standard Windows image viewers.
2026-04-06 12:11:39 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-06 12:11:39 [gemini-3.1-pro] In the GIF LZW specification, the encoder must increase its bit width exactly when the
2026-04-06 12:11:39 [gemini-3.1-pro] dictionary size reaches the current bit capacity (e.g., when `nextCode` hits 32 for a 5-bit width).
2026-04-06 12:11:39 [gemini-3.1-pro] Your implementation waits until it strictly exceeds the capacity (`>` instead of `===`), causing it
2026-04-06 12:11:39 [gemini-3.1-pro] to write one code too many at the smaller bit width. This desynchronizes the Chromium decoder and
2026-04-06 12:11:40 [gemini-3.1-pro] causes the loading error.
2026-04-06 12:11:40 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-06 12:11:40 [gemini-3.1-pro] Additionally, you need to cap the maximum bit width at 12 to prevent it from rolling over to 13
2026-04-06 12:11:40 [gemini-3.1-pro] when the dictionary reaches 4096.
