2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] The provided GIF encoder implementation has a significant architectural issue: your `Pixmap16`
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] class uses a bit-packed format (4 bits per pixel, stored in `Uint32Array`), but the `LzwEncoder` is
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] designed to process an 8-bit-per-pixel (`Uint8Array`) stream. Furthermore, the GIF format requires
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] the "Global Color Table" to be a power of two (2^n+1), and your palette has 16 entries, which is
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] correct, but your `begin` method sets the global color table bit depth incorrectly for a 16-color
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] palette.
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] Here are the specific corrections needed:
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1. Fix the Global Color Table Descriptor
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] In `begin()`, the byte `0xB3` (`10110011`) indicates a 256-color table. For 16 colors (4 bits), you
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] need to set the size bits correctly.
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] // Replace in begin()
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] // 0x80: Global Color Table present
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] // 0x03: Size of table (2^(3+1) = 16)
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] buf[4] = 0x83;
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2. Fix the LZW Data Stream
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] Your `LzwEncoder` expects a `Uint8Array` of bytes where each byte is a pixel index. Since your
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] `Pixmap16` already handles bit-packing, you should refactor `addFrame` to feed the `LzwEncoder` the
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] raw 4-bit values directly from the `point4` method.
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 3. Adjust the LZW Encoder Initialization
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] The GIF LZW specification requires the "Clear Code" to be 2^minCodeSize. Since your palette has 16
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] colors, the `minCodeSize` is 4 bits.
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] • Clear Code: 2⁴ = 16
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] • EOI Code: 17
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] Your current code uses `18` as the starting `nextCode`, which is correct, but the `BitPacker` needs
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] to ensure it starts with the correct `minCodeSize`.
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] Suggested Code Adjustment for `LzwEncoder`
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite] class LzwEncoder {
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     // ... existing properties ...
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]     encode(pixels: Uint8Array): Uint8Array {
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]         const packer = new BitPacker();
2026-04-06 12:35:07 [gemini-3.1-lite]         // Min code size for 16 colors is 4. Clear code is 16.
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]         packer.write(16, 5);
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]         this.reset();
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]         // ... rest of logic ...
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     }
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     private reset() {
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]         this.dict.clear();
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]         this.nextCode = 18;
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]         this.bitWidth = 5; // Start at 4+1 bits
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite]     }
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] }
2026-04-06 12:35:08 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
