2026-04-06 15:13:56 [nitro@ryzen5] rightmask of rect is not quite right
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] The issue with the `rightMask` logic in your `rect` function stems from how the bits are shifted
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] and aligned within the 32-bit word. Specifically, `0xFFFFFFFF << (28 - (4 * ((x + w - 1) & 7)))`
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] can result in a shift amount that exceeds 31 if not handled carefully, or produces the incorrect
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] bit pattern for the right-side boundary.
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] A more robust approach is to calculate the mask based on the number of nibbles (4-bit chunks) that
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] need to be cleared/set at the end of the line.
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] Here is the corrected `rect` method:
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, c4: number): void {
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		if (w <= 0 || h <= 0) return;
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		const c32 = c4 * 0x11111111;
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		const x0 = x >> 3;
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		const x1 = (x + w - 1) >> 3;
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		// Calculate masks for the start and end of the span
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		// Left mask: 1s from the start bit to the end of the word
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		const leftMask = 0xFFFFFFFF >>> (4 * (x & 7));
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		// Right mask: 1s from the start of the word to the end bit
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		const rightMask = 0xFFFFFFFF << (4 * (7 - ((x + w - 1) & 7)));
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		for (let row = y; row < y + h; row++) {
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 			const pos = row * this.span;
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 			if (x0 === x1) {
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 				// Single word case: intersection of both masks
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 				const mask = leftMask & rightMask;
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 				this.pix4[pos + x0] = (this.pix4[pos + x0] & ~mask) | (c32 & mask);
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 			} else {
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 				// Multi-word case: start, middle, and end
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 				this.pix4[pos + x0] = (this.pix4[pos + x0] & ~leftMask) | (c32 & leftMask);
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 				for (let i = x0 + 1; i < x1; i++) {
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 					this.pix4[pos + i] = c32;
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 				}
2026-04-06 15:14:03 [gemini-3.1-lite] 				this.pix4[pos + x1] = (this.pix4[pos + x1] & ~rightMask) | (c32 & rightMask);
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] 			}
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] 		}
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] 	}
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] Key Changes:
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] 1.  `rightMask` Logic: Changed to `0xFFFFFFFF << (4 * (7 - ((x + w - 1) & 7)))`.
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   `(x + w - 1) & 7` gives the index (0-7) of the last nibble.
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite]     *   `7 - index` gives the number of nibbles to shift left to position the 1s correctly at the
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] end of the word.
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] 2.  Clarity: By treating the masks as "everything to the right" (left mask) and "everything
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] to the left" (right mask), the intersection logic for the single-word case (`x0 === x1`) becomes
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] much cleaner and mathematically sound.
2026-04-06 15:14:04 [gemini-3.1-lite] 
