2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 6. PIO Architecture & Data Pipeline
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] To maintain a strict 16-bit per pixel memory bandwidth without utilizing the CPU, the architecture
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] employs a multi-stage State Machine (SM) pipeline linked by DMA channels.
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 6.1 The Multi-SM Pipeline
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1.  Broadcast DMA: A single DMA channel reads the 16-bit packed framebuffer and broadcasts
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] it to the TX FIFOs of the dedicated "Expander" State Machines.
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2.  Expander SMs (Bit-to-PDM): Each Expander SM strips its specific 3-bit payload, executes
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] a computed jump to generate a symmetric 10-bit PDM pattern, and pushes it to its RX FIFO.
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3.  Bridge DMAs: Dedicated memory-to-memory DMA channels move the generated 10-bit patterns
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] from the Expander RX FIFOs to the Output SM TX FIFOs.
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 4.  Output SMs: Synchronized "dumb" shifters that clock the 10-bit patterns to the physical
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] pins at the 148.5 MHz system clock.
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 6.2 Expander State Machine (PIO)
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] This program converts a 3-bit color/luma index into a 10-cycle, high-frequency symmetric PDM
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] pattern. It fits within 28 instructions.
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] .program expander
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; --- Computed Jump Table (Addresses 0-7) ---
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp p0
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp p1
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp p2
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp p3
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp p4
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp p5
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp p6
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp p7
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; --- Main Loop ---
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] public start:
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	; (C code configures 'out null, N' here if bit-stripping is required)
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out pc, 3            ; Pull 3 bits and jump to absolute address 0-7
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; --- Pattern Generation ---
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] p0:	set x, 0b00000 \ jmp emit  ; Level 0 (0%)
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] p1:	set x, 0b00010 \ jmp emit  ; Level 1 (~20%)
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] p2:	set x, 0b01010 \ jmp emit  ; Level 2 (~40%)
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] p3:	set x, 0b01011 \ jmp emit  ; Level 3 (~60%)
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] p4:	set x, 0b10101 \ jmp emit  ; Level 4 (50% Center)
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] p5:	set x, 0b10110 \ jmp emit  ; Level 5 (~60%)
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] p6:	set x, 0b11101 \ jmp emit  ; Level 6 (~80%)
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] p7:	set x, 0b11111             ; Level 7 (100% - Falls through)
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] emit:
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	in x, 5              ; Shift 5 bits into ISR
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	in x, 5              ; Shift SAME 5 bits again for 10-bit symmetry
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	push                 ; Send to RX FIFO for the Bridge DMA
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp start            ; Loop back for next pixel
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 6.3 Output State Machine (PIO)
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] This program runs on the physical output pins (Luma+, Pb, Pr, Trim). It is synchronized to the
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] `vidblit` base Luma IRQ to maintain perfect alignment with horizontal and vertical blanking.
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] .program output_shifter
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] .wrap_target
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	wait 1 irq 0         ; Wait for vidblit to enter active video
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] active_loop:
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pull block           ; Get 10-bit pattern from Bridge DMA
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out pins, 10         ; Shift out 10-cycle pattern to physical pin
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp pin, active_loop ; Monitor IRQ pin; loop if still in active video
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set pins, 0          ; Force 0V output during blanking/sync
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] .wrap
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:22:17 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:27:29 [nitro@ryzen5] i don't follow the expander code, what is public start meadoes public start mean
2026-04-07 16:27:39 [nitro@ryzen5] what does set \ jmp mean?
2026-04-07 16:27:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] `public start:`
2026-04-07 16:27:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] The `public` keyword makes the label visible to your C/C++ code.
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] When you compile this with `pioasm`, it generates a C constant (e.g.,
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] `expanderoffsetstart`). You pass this constant to the `piosminit()` function so the
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] State Machine knows to begin execution exactly at the main loop, safely skipping over the jump
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] table at the top of the file.
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] `set \ jmp`
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] This was a formatting error on my part. I used the `\` character to compress two instructions onto
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] a single line to save vertical space in the documentation.
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] Standard `pioasm` does not support this. They must be written as separate instructions on separate
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] lines. Here is the corrected, valid PIO syntax for that section:
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; --- Pattern Generation ---
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] p0:
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro]     set x, 0b00000
2026-04-07 16:27:55 [gemini-3.1-pro]     jmp emit  ; Level 0 (0%)
