2026-04-07 17:30:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] Why this is the ultimate solution:
2026-04-07 17:30:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Perfect 10-Cycle Timing: 9 `out` instructions + 1 `set` instruction = exactly 10 clock
2026-04-07 17:30:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] cycles per pixel.
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Free Blanking Synchronization: At the end of the active line, your DMA channel stops
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] sending pixels. The State Machine wraps around to the first `out pins, 1` and stalls
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] because the FIFO is empty.
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. Perfect 0V Porches: Because it stalls immediately after executing `set pins, 0`,
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] the physical pin freezes at 0V for the entire duration of the horizontal blanking period. When the
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] DMA starts the next line, the stall breaks and active video resumes instantly.
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] You have completely eliminated the need for IRQs, `wait` instructions, and `jmp` checks on the
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] output stage.
2026-04-07 17:30:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
