2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] Here's a rundown of the Raspberry Pi RP2350 specs:
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] Core
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - Dual-core ARM Cortex-M33 @ 150 MHz
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - Dual-core RISC-V Hazard3 @ 150 MHz (user-selectable at boot)
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - ARM and RISC-V cores cannot run simultaneously
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] Memory
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - 520 KB SRAM (10 banks)
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - External QSPI flash support (up to 64 MB via XIP)
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] GPIO
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - 48 GPIO pins (30 LPIO + 18 HPIO)
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] Peripherals
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - 2 × UART
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - 2 × SPI
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - 2 × I2C
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - 24 × PWM channels
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - 1 × USB 1.1 host/device
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - 4 × PIO state machines (Programmable I/O, same as RP2040)
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] ADC
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] - 4-channel 12-bit ADC
2026-04-08 15:53:43 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] Security
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] - ARM TrustZone support
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] - OTP (One-Time Programmable) memory
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] - Secure boot
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] - Hardware hash (SHA-256)
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] Other
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] - 2 × HSTX (High-Speed Transmit) lanes for driving displays
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] - Low-power sleep / dormant modes
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] - 40 nm process node
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] - QFN-60 package
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] It's essentially the RP2040's bigger sibling — dual-architecture (ARM + RISC-V), more memory,
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] better security, and HSTX for display interfacing.
2026-04-08 15:53:44 [glm-5.1] 
