2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] Look at the completions path in `relay()`:
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] const cached=usage.cache_tokens||usage.prompt_tokens_details?.cached_tokens||0;
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] That only checks two field names. Different providers return cached tokens differently:
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] - DeepSeek: `usage.promptcachehit_tokens` — not checked
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] - Anthropic: returns `cachetokens` (mapped in your adapter), but you only set
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] `cachecontrol: {type: "ephemeral"}` on file blocks, not on system messages — so Anthropic
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] likely never caches the system prompt
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] - OpenAI: needs explicit `cache_breakpoint` in the prompt to trigger caching
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] - Gemini: `cachedContentTokenCount` is mapped to `cache_tokens` — should work if Gemini
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] actually caches
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] The fix for DeepSeek is straightforward — add the missing field check:
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] const cached = usage.cache_tokens
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 	|| usage.prompt_tokens_details?.cached_tokens
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 	|| usage.prompt_cache_hit_tokens
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 	|| 0;
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] 
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] Which provider are you seeing zeros on? That'll narrow down whether it's a field name mismatch or
2026-04-08 16:18:25 [glm-5.1] caching not being triggered at all.
