2026-04-17 20:21:28 [gemini-3.1-pro] lost.
2026-04-17 20:21:28 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:21:28 [gemini-3.1-pro] Because both the Video state machine and the Teletext state machine are driving the exact same
2026-04-17 20:21:28 [gemini-3.1-pro] physical video output, `WSTPIN` is just exactly the same as `VIDPIN` (GP28).
2026-04-17 20:21:28 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:21:28 [gemini-3.1-pro] You can simply update your `wstinit` function to use `VIDPIN` for both the `set` and `out`
2026-04-17 20:21:28 [gemini-3.1-pro] pin mappings. This directly maps the `set pins, 0` instruction in your PIO assembly to GP28.
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is the updated `wst_init` function:
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] void wst_init(PIO pio, int sm) {
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	const pio_program_t *program2 = &wst_program;
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	uint offset2 = pio_add_program(pio, program2);
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_config config2 = wst_program_get_default_config(offset2);
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Map both 'set' and 'out' instructions to GP28
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	sm_config_set_set_pins(&config2, VID_PIN, 1);
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	sm_config_set_out_pins(&config2, VID_PIN, 1);
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Shift Right = true, Autopull = false
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	sm_config_set_out_shift(&config2, true, false, 32);
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	sm_config_set_fifo_join(&config2, PIO_FIFO_JOIN_TX);
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Set clock to exactly 13.875 MHz (2 cycles per bit = 6.9375 Mbps)
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	sm_config_set_clkdiv(&config2, 10.7027f);
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	int pioStatus = pio_sm_init(pio, sm, offset2, &config2);
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_set_enabled(pio, sm, true);
2026-04-17 20:21:29 [gemini-3.1-pro] }
