2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] This looks absolutely fantastic. The structure is incredibly clean, and moving both the video and
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] the data streams to parallel DMA channels is the hallmark of a highly optimized embedded system.
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] Before you compile and test, I spotted one tiny DMA gotcha in the `vid_field` function that we need
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] to catch!
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] When a DMA channel finishes a transfer, its internal transfer counter hits `0`. If you try to
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] trigger it again by just setting the read address, it will immediately halt because it thinks it
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] has 0 words left to move.
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] You correctly handled this for the `videodmachan` by calling
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] `dmachannelsettranscount(..., false)` right before setting the read address. We
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] just need to do the exact same thing for the new `wstdmachan` so it knows to send exactly
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 15 words every field.
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is the quick fix for your `vid_field` function:
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] void vid_field(int field) {
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	if (field & 1) {
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		// Dispatch Odd Video Field
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		dma_channel_set_trans_count(video_dma_chan, wordCount + words, false);
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		dma_channel_set_read_addr(video_dma_chan, oddFrame, true);
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		// Dispatch Odd Teletext Field (15 words)
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		dma_channel_set_trans_count(wst_dma_chan, 15, false);
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		dma_channel_set_read_addr(wst_dma_chan, wstOdd, true);
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	} else {
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		// Dispatch Even Video Field
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		dma_channel_set_trans_count(video_dma_chan, wordCount, false);
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		dma_channel_set_read_addr(video_dma_chan, evenFrame, true);
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		// Dispatch Even Teletext Field (15 words)
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		dma_channel_set_trans_count(wst_dma_chan, 15, false);
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		dma_channel_set_read_addr(wst_dma_chan, wstEven, true);
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	}
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] }
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] Once you add those two `dmachannelsettranscount` lines, the DMA will continuously
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] pump the Teletext commands into the PIO every single frame without fail.
2026-04-17 20:27:49 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
