2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] Unlike some other microcontrollers, the RP2350's PIO `wait` instruction does not clear the
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] IRQ flag.
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] Because I left out the instruction to clear it, here is exactly what your RP2350 just did:
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Video SM fires `irq set 0` on Line 0.
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Teletext SM wakes up and transmits its packet.
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. Teletext SM loops back to `wait 1 irq 0`.
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] 4. Because the flag was never cleared, it is still 1.
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] 5. The Teletext SM immediately wakes back up and transmits again... and again... and again!
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] The Teletext state machine was "free-running" at maximum speed, constantly blasting `1`s onto
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] `pindirs` during the Front Porch, during the HSYNC, and during the Back Porch of every single line.
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] It completely obliterated the video sync.
2026-04-17 20:38:45 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
