2026-04-17 21:51:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] Why this PIO loop is brilliant
2026-04-17 21:51:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] In your `wst.pio`, the `pull block` instruction explicitly overwrites the Output Shift Register
2026-04-17 21:51:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] (OSR). This means any leftover padding bits from the 12th payload word are instantly flushed into
2026-04-17 21:51:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] the void at the start of the next line, ensuring perfect byte alignment every single time.
2026-04-17 21:51:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
