2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] That is excellent news. With the video stable and the PIO architecture locked in, we can move
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] entirely into C++ data generation.
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] To make the TV recognize the page, we need to send a Page Header (Row 0). This requires
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] calculating Hamming 8/4 codes for the routing data, and Odd Parity for the text
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] characters.
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here are the reusable C++ functions to generate perfectly encoded WST data.
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] Add these lookup tables and functions above your `initTeletext()` function:
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] // Pre-calculated Hamming 8/4 encoding table
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] const uint8_t HAMMING_84[16] = {
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	0x15, 0x02, 0x49, 0x5E, 0x64, 0x73, 0x38, 0x2F,
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	0xD0, 0xC7, 0x8C, 0x9B, 0xA1, 0xB6, 0xFD, 0xEA
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] };
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] // Calculates Odd Parity for standard text characters
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] uint8_t odd_parity(char c) {
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	uint8_t b = c & 0x7F;
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	uint8_t parity = 1;
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	for (int i = 0; i < 7; i++) {
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		if (b & (1 << i)) parity ^= 1;
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	}
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	return b | (parity << 7);
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] }
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] // Builds a perfectly formatted 45-byte Page Header and packs it into 12 words
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] void build_wst_header(int mag, int page_tens, int page_units, const char* text, uint32_t* out_words) {
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	uint8_t packet[45];
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	packet[0] = 0x55; packet[1] = 0x55; packet[2] = 0xE4; // Clock Run-In & Framing
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Magazine and Row Address (Row = 0 for Header)
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mag &= 7;
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	packet[3] = HAMMING_84[mag & 1];
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	packet[4] = HAMMING_84[(mag >> 1) & 3];
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Page Number (Tens and Units)
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	packet[5] = HAMMING_84[page_units & 0xF];
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	packet[6] = HAMMING_84[page_tens & 0xF];
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Subcode (0000) and Control Bits (Defaults)
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	packet[7] = HAMMING_84[0]; packet[8] = HAMMING_84[0];
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	packet[9] = HAMMING_84[0]; packet[10] = HAMMING_84[0];
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	packet[11] = HAMMING_84[0]; packet[12] = HAMMING_84[0];
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// 32 characters of Header Text
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	for (int i = 0; i < 32; i++) {
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		char c = (text && text[i]) ? text[i] : ' ';
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		packet[13 + i] = odd_parity(c);
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	}
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Pack the 45 bytes into the 12 uint32_t DMA words (LSB first)
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	for (int i = 0; i < 12; i++) {
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		out_words[i] = 0;
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		for (int b = 0; b < 4; b++) {
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			int idx = (i * 4) + b;
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			if (idx < 45) {
2026-04-17 22:09:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 				out_words[i] |= (uint32_t)packet[idx] << (b * 8);
2026-04-17 22:09:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] 			}
2026-04-17 22:09:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] 		}
2026-04-17 22:09:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	}
2026-04-17 22:09:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] }
2026-04-17 22:09:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:09:02 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
