2026-04-17 22:29:58 [gemini-3.1-pro] The "Perfect PAL" Interlace Trick
2026-04-17 22:29:58 [gemini-3.1-pro] While looking at your deduction, I realized we can make the TV timing even better.
2026-04-17 22:29:58 [gemini-3.1-pro] A true PAL frame is exactly 625 lines.
2026-04-17 22:29:58 [gemini-3.1-pro] If we make both fields exactly 312.5 lines (312.5 + 312.5 = 625), the 0.5 remainder
2026-04-17 22:29:58 [gemini-3.1-pro] will cause the PIO's HSYNC phase to naturally invert every single field. This creates a
2026-04-17 22:29:58 [gemini-3.1-pro] mathematically perfect, broadcast-spec interlaced signal!
2026-04-17 22:29:58 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-17 22:29:58 [gemini-3.1-pro] To get 312.5 lines, we just make the VSYNC pulse exactly 3.5 lines long (33,263 cycles) for
2026-04-17 22:29:58 [gemini-3.1-pro] both fields.
