2026-04-17 23:42:08 [kimi-k2.5] If any character has wrong parity, the TV typically displays a space or block. Verify `oddParity`
2026-04-17 23:42:08 [kimi-k2.5] is generating the correct bit. For example, space (0x20 = 00100000) has two 1s (even), so parity
2026-04-17 23:42:08 [kimi-k2.5] bit should be 1 to make odd. Your function starts with `parity = 1` and XORs, so:
2026-04-17 23:42:08 [kimi-k2.5] - 0x20: bits 5 set. Loop runs, parity ^= 1 (bit 5) → parity = 0. Result: 0x20 | 0x80 = 0xA0.
2026-04-17 23:42:08 [kimi-k2.5] Correct (odd parity).
