2026-04-17 23:45:21 [kimi-k2.5] The `wst_init` function enables autopull (`true` in the third parameter), but your PIO
2026-04-17 23:45:21 [kimi-k2.5] program uses explicit `pull,block`. This causes a conflict where the hardware autopulls one word
2026-04-17 23:45:21 [kimi-k2.5] while the instruction pulls another, skipping every other word in the FIFO.
2026-04-17 23:45:21 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] Change this line in `wst_init`:
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] sm_config_set_out_shift(&config2, true, false, 32);  // Disable autopull
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] The explicit `pull,block` in your PIO program is correct for this state machine because you need to
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] load `x` with the bit count before entering the loop. Autopull would interfere by automatically
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] refilling the OSR after exactly 32 shifts, which happens mid-packet (after the first 32 bits),
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] causing the subsequent `pull` to grab the wrong word.
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] • Why this causes missing characters:*
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] With autopull enabled, the sequence becomes:
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 1. First `pull` grabs command word (368)
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 2. First 32 bits shift out (bytes 0-3 of packet)
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 3. Autopull grabs next word (bytes 4-7) automatically
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 4. Explicit `pull` at top of loop grabs word after that (bytes 8-11), skipping bytes 4-7
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 5. This continues, causing every 4-byte chunk to be shifted by one position
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] The TV sees valid Clock Run-In and Framing Code (early bytes), but the Header Text (bytes 14-45)
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] gets scrambled parity, so it displays spaces for corrupted characters.
2026-04-17 23:45:22 [kimi-k2.5] 
