2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] The missing characters are caused by autopull discarding the final 16 bits of your 368-bit
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] packet.
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] With autopull enabled (`smconfigsetoutshift(&config2, true, true, 32)`), the state
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] machine automatically refills the Output Shift Register (OSR) every 32 bits. When your loop
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] finishes after shifting 368 bits, there are 16 bits remaining in the OSR (bits 16-31 of the
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] 12th word). The next `pull block` at the top of the program discards those 16 bits to load the next
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] command.
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] 368 bits = 46 bytes. Your packet layout:
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] - Bytes 0-43: Clock run-in, framing, addresses, first 30 header characters
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] - Bytes 44-45: Last 2 header characters (positions 30 and 31)
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] - Bytes 46-47: Zero padding
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:58:35 [kimi-k2.5] The autopull discard drops bytes 44-45, chopping off the last 2 characters of your header text.
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] • Quick fix:* Send only 352 bits (11 words = 44 bytes), dropping the last 2 characters.
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] Since your header `" TOUCHGRASS WST GENERATOR 2026  "` ends with 2 spaces (positions 30-31), you
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] won't see any difference:
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] wstEven[p++] = 352;  // 44 bytes = 11 words
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] • Proper fix:* Disable autopull and manually pull words in the loop, or pad the DMA buffer
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] to a multiple of 32 bits and accept that the final 16 bits extend into the porch (but during porch,
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] `vidblit` has `pins=0`, so any `1` bits become `0`, corrupting the signal).
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-17 23:58:36 [kimi-k2.5] The 352-bit fix is the path of least resistance here.
