2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] The comment says:
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	or lines with 368 bit payload additional 16 bits padding empties fifo
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] That means each active line consumes:
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] - 32-bit command word
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] - 368 payload bits
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] - 16 extra bits
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] So total consumed from FIFO after the command is 384 bits = 12 words.
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 06:42:49 [gpt-5.4-2026] That matches your 12 packed words exactly.
