2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] I do not think that is correct teletext packet addressing.
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] For packet 0, row 0, magazine 1, you want the address nibbles, then Hamming encode them.
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] Conceptually:
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] - first nibble = magazine + row LSB
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] - second nibble = remaining row bits
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] For row 0 that reduces to:
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] - first nibble = `mag`
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] - second nibble = `0`
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] So I would expect:
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] int row = 0;
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] int addr1 = (mag & 0x7) | ((row & 0x1) << 3);
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] int addr2 = (row >> 1) & 0xF;
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] packet[4] = HAMMING_84[addr1];
2026-04-18 07:00:44 [gpt-5.4-2026] packet[5] = HAMMING_84[addr2];
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] With `mag = 1`, that becomes:
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] - `packet[4] = HAMMING_84[1]`
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] - `packet[5] = HAMMING_84[0]`
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] Your current code instead produces:
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] - `packet[4] = HAMMING_84[1]`
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] - `packet[5] = HAMMING_84[0]` for mag 1 by coincidence
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] So for magazine 1 only, your current code happens to match that case.
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] That means the address bug is still real in general, but for your current test page it may not be
2026-04-18 07:00:45 [gpt-5.4-2026] the immediate cause.
