2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] A problem that:
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] - sometimes looks clean
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] - then becomes rough again
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] - without major code changes
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] is usually not a deterministic field-layout bug.
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] It is more often one of:
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 1. burst start timing is near the decoder threshold
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 2. signal amplitude / level is marginal
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 3. line placement is marginal
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 4. PIO/video interaction causes slight phase variation
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 5. the TV decoder needs repeated consistent packets to settle, and your stream is only barely
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] valid
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] So I’d now put much less weight on packet 0 control bits, and much more on physical timing and
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] placement.
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] Important context from your setup
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] You are generating teletext by modulating pin direction on the same composite output pin
2026-04-18 07:12:27 [gpt-5.4-2026] used for video.
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] That is elegant, but it is also fragile because teletext decoding depends on a fairly clean
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] high-frequency waveform riding at the correct video level.
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] If the output level depends on:
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] - GPIO output latch state
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] - high-Z vs drive
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] - resistor network
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] - concurrent video timing
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] - TV termination
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] then small variations can easily produce “sometimes good, sometimes rough”.
