2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] Why the first clean result may have been misleading
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] Teletext decoders often cache and average over repeated fields. A momentary good-looking decode
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] does not necessarily mean the packet format is fully correct; it may just mean the set happened to
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] lock better for a moment.
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:12:28 [gpt-5.4-2026] So “first test clean, second rough” is classic marginal-lock behaviour.
