2026-04-18 07:22:42 [nitro@ryzen5] is there a sm_config_set_clkdiv_int_frac8 version that would give us better accuracy, varying float does not seem to have much affect
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] Yes — there is an integer/fractional divider form, but in your case it will not buy you
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] meaningfully more accuracy than the exact value you already have.
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] Short answer
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] Use:
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] sm_config_set_clkdiv_int_frac8(&config2, 10, 180);
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] because:
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 10 + 180/256 = 10.703125
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] That is the nearest 16.8 fixed-point divider to:
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 148.5 / 13.875 = 10.7027027027...
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] But important point
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] That is not actually more accurate than the float API in any practical sense.
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] On RP PIO, the divider is implemented as a fixed-point hardware value anyway. The float call is
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] just converted to the same sort of register representation.
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] So if changing the float slightly has little effect, that strongly suggests:
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] - you are already close enough on bit rate
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] - the real problem is elsewhere
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] The exact numbers
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] Target SM frequency:
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 13.875 MHz
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] With system clock:
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 148.5 MHz
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] Required divider:
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 148.5 / 13.875 = 10.7027027027...
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] Nearest `int.frac8` choices:
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] - `10 + 179/256 = 10.69921875`
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] - `10 + 180/256 = 10.703125`
2026-04-18 07:22:55 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] `10 + 180/256` is closer.
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] Resulting SM clock
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 148.5 / 10.703125 ≈ 13.874453
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] Error is tiny.
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] Why float tweaking may appear to do nothing
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] Because the hardware divider has limited resolution, a range of nearby float values may quantise to
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] the same underlying divider setting.
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] So:
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] sm_config_set_clkdiv(&config2, 10.7026f);
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] sm_config_set_clkdiv(&config2, 10.7027f);
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] sm_config_set_clkdiv(&config2, 10.7028f);
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] may all end up programming the same effective divider.
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] That would explain why small float changes seem to have no effect.
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] Recommendation
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] If you want deterministic control, use:
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] sm_config_set_clkdiv_int_frac8(&config2, 10, 180);
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] But I would treat that as a clarity improvement, not a likely fix.
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] What this implies diagnostically
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] If divider nudging barely changes behaviour, then your remaining issue is more likely:
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] - burst placement in the line
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] - signal level / waveform
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] - preamble/framing alignment
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] - interaction of WST modulation with the composite output method
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] rather than raw bit-rate error.
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] Practical takeaway
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] Yes, there is an `int_frac8` form, and the best setting is:
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] sm_config_set_clkdiv_int_frac8(&config2, 10, 180);
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] But I would not expect a dramatic improvement from it.
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] If you want, I can help calculate the horizontal timing of your WST burst relative to the PAL
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] line from your current video PIO so we can see whether the packet is landing in the right part
2026-04-18 07:22:56 [gpt-5.4-2026] of the VBI.
