2026-04-18 07:25:41 [nitro@ryzen5] my monochrome video out does not generate a color burst, does that impact anything
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] Not for teletext, no.
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] A TV does not need a PAL colour burst to decode WST teletext. Teletext is carried as
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] high-speed luminance-domain data in the VBI, and monochrome composite video is enough in principle.
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] So lack of colour burst should not stop teletext working
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] You can have:
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - valid sync
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - valid line timing
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - no chroma burst
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - black-and-white picture
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] and teletext can still work.
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] But there is a nuance
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] While the colour burst itself is not required for teletext decoding, some TVs behave better
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] when the incoming signal looks like a more conventional broadcast composite waveform.
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] So lack of burst usually does not break teletext directly, but on some sets it may
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] indirectly affect how happily the decoder locks to the signal.
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] In practice:
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - many TVs will decode teletext fine on monochrome composite
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - some TVs may be fussier about nonstandard VBI/video conditions
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] In your case
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] Because the TV is already:
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - recognising teletext
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - showing a header at least sometimes
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] the absence of colour burst is clearly not the primary problem.
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] Your problem is more likely still one of:
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - teletext burst placement
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - packet alignment
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - signal amplitude / waveform shape
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - line selection
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] Short answer
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - Does no colour burst prevent teletext? No.
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - Could it slightly affect decoder tolerance on some TVs? Possibly.
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] - Is it likely your main issue here? No.
2026-04-18 07:25:50 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:25:51 [gpt-5.4-2026] If you want, I can help estimate whether your teletext burst is landing at the correct horizontal
2026-04-18 07:25:51 [gpt-5.4-2026] position within the PAL line, which is probably more relevant.
2026-04-18 07:25:51 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:26:40 [nitro@ryzen5] yes please
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] Yes. Based on your current PIOs, the teletext burst is starting far too early in the line.
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] That is the biggest thing I’d fix next.
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] Where your WST starts now
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] In `vidblit.pio`:
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] line:
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	set	pindirs, 0
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	set	pins, 1
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	; active = 51.71 µs = 7,680 cycles
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	mov	y,isr
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	irq	set 0
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] active:
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	out	pindirs, 1 [8]
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	jmp	y--,active
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] The key point is:
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] irq set 0
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] This happens right at the start of active video.
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] In `wst.pio`:
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] out	x, 32
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] wait	1 irq 0
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] irq	clear 0
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] jmp	!x start
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] bit_loop:
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	out	pindirs, 1
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 	jmp	x-- bit_loop
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] So the teletext state machine begins transmitting essentially immediately after the start of
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] active video.
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] Why that is wrong for teletext
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] Teletext data belongs in the VBI line, not at the start of active picture.
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] The packet should begin roughly 10–12 µs after the leading edge of line sync, i.e. in the
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] blanking interval before visible picture.
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] Your current trigger point is after:
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] - sync
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] - back porch
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] - and right at active picture start
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] So you are already about 10.5 µs too late relative to sync, and then your packet begins
2026-04-18 07:27:08 [gpt-5.4-2026] immediately from there.
2026-04-18 07:27:09 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:09 [gpt-5.4-2026] That means the teletext burst is landing around the start of visible video, not in the intended VBI
2026-04-18 07:27:09 [gpt-5.4-2026] insertion window.
2026-04-18 07:27:09 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:27:09 [gpt-5.4-2026] A tolerant decoder may still find it sometimes, which matches your symptoms.
2026-04-18 07:27:09 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
