2026-04-18 07:46:17 [nitro@ryzen5] nop[20] header is consistently blank
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] That’s useful: it means you’ve moved the packet too late. The fix is to start
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] earlier, not later.
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] Why
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] Your `wait 1 irq 0` is already keyed from the start of active video in `vidblit.pio`:
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] mov	y,isr
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] irq	set 0
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] active:
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] So adding `nop [20]` in `wst.pio` delays the teletext burst by about 1.51 µs, pushing it
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] further into/after the decoder’s expected window. A consistently blank header means the TV no
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] longer sees a valid packet there.
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] Best next move
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] Trigger the WST earlier relative to the line, i.e. from back porch, not from active
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] start.
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] Easiest clean fix
2026-04-18 07:46:29 [gpt-5.4-2026] Move the IRQ in `vidblit.pio` into the back porch at a chosen point.
