2026-04-18 07:51:14 [nitro@ryzen5] doesnt backporch need to be solid black?
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] Yes — normally the back porch should stay clean black/blanking level.
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] So as a general design point, you do not really want teletext data in the back porch
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] itself.
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] That is an important correction.
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] More precise view
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] A teletext line is typically:
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] - sync
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] - back porch / blanking
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] - then teletext data burst in the line blanking interval before active picture
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] - still not in visible picture
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] So the teletext packet is not meant to overwrite the sync pulse, and you generally want the
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] decoder to see a sane blanking region.
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] But in practice the teletext data sits in the horizontal blanking interval after sync, not in the
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] visible image.
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] So when we said “move it into back porch”, that was shorthand for:
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] - launch it earlier relative to active video
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] - so it lands in the proper blanked VBI data region
2026-04-18 07:51:30 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] not “smear data across the whole back porch”.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] In your implementation
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] Because the WST stream starts immediately on IRQ, moving the IRQ earlier directly moves the packet
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] into blanking.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] That can work for testing, but yes, ideally the blanking interval should still be well-formed and
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] the teletext packet should start at the proper point within it.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] Better way to think about it
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] You want:
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - line sync intact
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - some blanking after sync
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - CRI + framing + packet
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - all before visible picture begins
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] So the real control variable is:
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] packet start time relative to sync edge
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] not “put data in back porch” as such.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] Answer to your question
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - Does back porch need to be solid black? Generally yes.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - Can teletext occupy part of the horizontal blanking interval before active video? Yes.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - Should it clobber the whole porch arbitrarily? No.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] What this means for your tuning
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] Your current trigger at active-video start is probably too late.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] But moving the trigger all the way to the start of back porch may be too early.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] So the right solution is likely:
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - trigger from a known line reference
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - then delay so the CRI begins at the correct point after sync
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] That gives you proper blanking before the packet and keeps it out of visible video.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] Best architectural fix
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] Instead of using the start of active video as the reference, or stuffing the burst directly into
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] back porch by trial and error, do this:
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 1. raise the IRQ at a stable reference point in the line, ideally near sync end or back-porch start
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 2. add a controlled delay in `wst.pio`
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 3. start the packet after that delay
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] That way:
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - sync stays intact
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - initial porch stays black
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] - teletext starts in the right part of the blanking interval
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] Why your earlier tests still helped
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] Even though “back porch should be black” is true, your experiments were still useful because they
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] proved timing sensitivity and bracketed the valid window.
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:31 [gpt-5.4-2026] Bottom line
2026-04-18 07:51:32 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:32 [gpt-5.4-2026] Yes, the porch should basically remain blank, and the teletext data should be positioned within the
2026-04-18 07:51:32 [gpt-5.4-2026] allowed horizontal blanking interval before active video, not just anywhere.
2026-04-18 07:51:32 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
2026-04-18 07:51:32 [gpt-5.4-2026] If you want, I can help you estimate a better target delay from your current PAL timing so the CRI
2026-04-18 07:51:32 [gpt-5.4-2026] lands around the proper ~10–12 µs-after-sync region.
2026-04-18 07:51:32 [gpt-5.4-2026] 
