2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] Yes — you are very close to the correct timing, but you are near the early edge of the decoder
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] window. Do not reduce the back porch — that would shift the burst earlier to ~9.7 µs, which
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] your tests already showed is too early (gives “Not Available”).
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] Instead, you should increase the back porch slightly and compensate by shortening the
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] active video on those VBI lines (which are black anyway).
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] Current timing analysis
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] From your `vidblit.pio`:
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] - Front porch: ~1.64 µs (243 cycles)
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] - Hsync: ~4.66 µs (692 cycles)
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] - Back porch: ~5.87 µs (872 cycles)
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] - Active starts at: ~10.53 µs from line start
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] Standard teletext expects the CRI to start roughly 10.5–12 µs from the line start. Your
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] current position (~10.53 µs) is at the very early edge of that window. Your tests confirm this:
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] - 4 back-porch chunks earlier (~0.8 µs earlier = ~9.7 µs): Fail (too early)
2026-04-18 08:10:37 [kimi-k2.5] - Current (~10.53 µs): Rough (marginal)
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] - `nop [20]` later (~1.5 µs later = ~12.0 µs): Fail (packet runs into next line’s sync)
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] The `nop [20]` fails because it delays the 53 µs packet so it ends at ~65.1 µs, overflowing the 64
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] µs line into the next sync pulse.
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] The fix
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] Shift the burst ~0.6 µs later to hit the ~11.1 µs sweet spot.
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] Since you cannot add delay to the WST without overflowing the line, instead move the IRQ
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] trigger later by increasing the back porch, and shorten the active video on VBI lines
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] to keep the line length at 64 µs.
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] Specific numbers
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] Add 3 back-porch chunks (~90 cycles @ 148.5 MHz = 0.606 µs):
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] In `vidblit.pio`, change the back porch loop count from 28 to 31, and add a compensating delay or
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] just accept the line is 0.6 µs longer for those lines (PAL tolerance is usually ±0.3 µs, but since
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] these are VBI lines, strict exactness matters less).
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] Better yet, since you generate the frame buffer in `initFrame()`, reduce the `pixelcounter` value
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] for the teletext-carrying lines by 90 cycles (9 iterations of your active loop, which does 10
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] cycles per iteration? Check your active loop timing).
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] Your active loop:
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] active:
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 	out	pindirs, 1 [8]
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 	jmp	y--,active
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] That’s 10 cycles per iteration (1 + 8 delay + 1).
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] So reduce the `pixelcounter` (the value loaded into `isr`) for lines 0–21 by 9 (90 cycles /
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 10).
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] Then increase back porch count by 3 (90 cycles).
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
