2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] - Teletext starts at ~11.14 µs (10.53 + 0.61)
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] - Packet ends at ~64.2 µs (still within 64 µs if you account for front porch starting the
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] next line, or accept tiny overflow into front porch which is usually tolerable)
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] - Active video on those lines is 9 iterations shorter (black anyway)
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] Alternative: shorten the preamble
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] If you prefer not to juggle line lengths, reduce your CRI from 3 bytes to 2 bytes (standard is 16
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] bits of 0x55, you currently have 24 bits). This saves 1.15 µs (1 byte = 8 bits × 2 cycles ×
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 72 ns).
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] Then you can add `nop [8]` or `nop [10]` in `wst.pio` to shift the whole packet ~0.6–0.7 µs later
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] without overflowing the line.
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] But adjusting the back porch and active count is cleaner.
2026-04-18 08:10:38 [kimi-k2.5] 
