2026-04-18 12:15:18 [nitro@ryzen5] sm_config_set_clkdiv_int_frac8 to gen 13.875mhz from 148.5mHz
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] To generate 13.875 MHz from a 148.5 MHz system clock, calculate the divider ratio:
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] \[
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] \frac{148.5}{13.875} = \frac{396}{37} \approx 10.7027
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] \]
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] Convert to 16.8 fixed-point (integer + fraction/256):
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] • Integer: 10
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] • Fraction: \(0.7027 \times 256 \approx 179.9\) → round to 180 (0xB4)
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] pio_sm_config config = pio_get_default_sm_config();
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] // 148.5 MHz / (10 + 180/256) ≈ 13.8746 MHz (error: ~-26 ppm)
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] sm_config_set_clkdiv_int_frac8(&config, 10, 180);
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] • Result:* 13.8746 MHz (365 Hz slow).
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] If you need the exact frequency and can tolerate jitter, consider using the floating-point variant
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] instead:
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] sm_config_set_clkdiv(&config, 148.5f / 13.875f);
2026-04-18 12:16:13 [kimi-k2.5] 
