2026-04-20 16:37:02 [nitro@ryzen5] what is arm cores in RP2350
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] • ARM Cores in the RP2350*
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] The RP2350 (used in the Raspberry Pi Pico 2) is a dual-core microcontroller, but unlike the
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] RP2040, it is not based on ARM cores.
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] RP2350 Core Configuration:
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] ╭────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] │  Feature                   │  RP2350 Specification                   │
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] ├────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] │  **Primary Cores**         │  **2× Cortex-M33** (ARM)                │
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] │  **Secondary Cores**       │  2× **Hazard3** (RISC-V)                │
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] │  Total Programmable Cores  │  **4 cores** (2 ARM + 2 RISC-V)         │
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] │  Architecture              │  ARMv8-M (for Cortex-M33)               │
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] ╰────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] Detailed Breakdown:
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] - 2 × Cortex-M33 (ARM cores)
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309]   - Clocked at up to 150 MHz
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309]   - ARMv8-M architecture
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309]   - Support for TrustZone (hardware security)
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309]   - Better performance and efficiency than the Cortex-M0+ used in RP2040
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309]   - Includes DSP instructions and floating-point unit (FPU)
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309] - 2 × Hazard3 (RISC-V cores)
2026-04-20 16:37:05 [grok-4.20-0309]   - These are open-source RISC-V cores designed by Raspberry Pi engineers.
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309]   - Also run at up to 150 MHz.
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309]   - You can choose at boot time whether to run the ARM cores or the RISC-V cores (you can't run all
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] 4 at the same time).
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] Summary:
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] - The ARM cores in the RP2350 are dual Cortex-M33 cores.
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] - This is a big upgrade from the RP2040’s dual Cortex-M0+ cores.
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] - The RP2350 is unique because it gives you the choice between running ARM (Cortex-M33) or
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] RISC-V (Hazard3) cores.
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] Would you like me to also explain how to choose between ARM and RISC-V mode when programming the
2026-04-20 16:37:06 [grok-4.20-0309] Pico 2?
