2026-04-20 16:39:31 [nitro@ryzen5] what thumb variant is supported in M33?
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] • Correct Answer:*
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] The Cortex-M33 in the RP2350 supports Thumb-2.
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] Detailed Breakdown:
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] ╭────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] │  Feature               │  Supported in Cortex-M33 (RP2350)  │  Notes                                │
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] ├────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] │  **Thumb**             │  Yes                               │  16-bit instructions                  │
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] │  **Thumb-2**           │  **Yes** (full support)            │  Both 16-bit and 32-bit instructions  │
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] │  ARM (32-bit) mode     │  No                                │  M33 is Thumb-only                    │
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] │  DSP extensions        │  Yes                               │  Part of Thumb-2                      │
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] ╰────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] What this means for RP2350:
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] - The Cortex-M33 cores use Thumb-2 exclusively.
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] - Thumb-2 is a superset of Thumb. It adds many 32-bit instructions while keeping the high code
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] density of 16-bit Thumb instructions.
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] - This is a significant upgrade compared to the Cortex-M0+ in the RP2040, which only supported the
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] original Thumb (no Thumb-2).
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] • Summary:*
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] The ARM cores in the RP2350 (Cortex-M33) support Thumb-2.
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] Would you like me to also show the difference in instruction sets between M0+ (RP2040) and M33
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] (RP2350)?
2026-04-20 16:39:34 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:22 [nitro@ryzen5] for my vm, i currently have a basic arm generator in developmentit was based on thumb
2026-04-20 16:44:45 [grok-4.20-0309] • Thank you for sharing the code.*
2026-04-20 16:44:45 [grok-4.20-0309] I’ve reviewed your `thumb2.h` carefully.
2026-04-20 16:44:45 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:45 [grok-4.20-0309] Honest Feedback:
2026-04-20 16:44:45 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:45 [grok-4.20-0309] Your current `thumb2` class is not actually generating Thumb-2.
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] It is still only generating original Thumb (the 16-bit only instructions from the
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] Cortex-M0/M0+ era).
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] This is the most important point:
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 	he Cortex-M33 in the RP2350 only executes Thumb-2.
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 	t does not support the original Thumb-only mode that the RP2040’s M0+ used.
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] Major Problems in your current file:
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 1. No 32-bit Thumb-2 instructions at all
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309]    You only have functions that return `u16`. Real Thumb-2 uses 32-bit instructions for many
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] important operations (especially `movw`, `movt`, `ldr.w`, `add.w`, `ldr.w pc-relative`, `blx`, `it`
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] blocks, etc.).
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 2. You are missing the high registers properly (R8–R12 are barely supported).
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 3. No support for the new instructions that Cortex-M33 added (e.g. `cbz`, `clz`, `rev`, `sdiv`,
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] `udiv`, `mla`, `mls`, `ldr.w`, `str.w`, etc.).
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:44:46 [grok-4.20-0309] 4. The comment at the top says `// 2026.4.20 and=>ands system=>memory thumb->thumb2` — this
