2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] I’ve read the new version you posted. Here are my honest observations, in order of importance:
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 1. Most Critical Issue (This is the main thing we should talk about first)
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] Even though the file is now named `thumb2.h` and the comment says “RP2350 CORTEX-M33 thumb2 code
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] generator”, the vast majority of the code is still generating classic Thumb (16-bit)
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] instructions, exactly the same as before.
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] The only two functions that actually emit Thumb-2 32-bit instructions are these:
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
