2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] u16 bl1(int off);
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] Everything else (`add`, `ldr`, `mov`, `ands`, `push`, `pop`, etc.) is still producing the old
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 16-bit Thumb encodings.
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] This is the core mismatch we need to discuss before we change anything.
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 2. Minor but noticeable changes
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] 
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] - You added `#include <stdint.h>` and `typedef uint32_t u32;` — good.
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] - You kept `typedef uint16_t u16;` — this is now potentially confusing because we will need 32-bit
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] values for real Thumb-2.
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] - The comment at the top now mentions RP2350 and Cortex-M33 — that’s accurate for the target, but
2026-04-20 16:52:29 [grok-4.20-0309] the implementation doesn’t yet match the claim.
