2026-04-20 20:16:58 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `IT` (only if you plan to use predicated narrow sequences; many JITs skip it)
2026-04-20 20:16:58 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `LDR literal (wide forms / flexibility)` if your constant/materialization strategy grows
2026-04-20 20:16:58 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `ADR` wide (address formation convenience)
2026-04-20 20:16:58 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `MRS/MSR` only if you need special registers (rare for user JIT)
2026-04-20 20:16:58 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `DMB/DSB/ISB` (important if you do self-modifying code and need robust I-cache/sync
2026-04-20 20:16:58 [gpt-5.3-codex] behavior on real targets)
2026-04-20 20:16:59 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `CLZ`, `REV`, `SXTB/SXTH/UXTB/UXTH` (common low-level ops that avoid helper calls)
