2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] I'll help you calculate the resistor value to replace the trimpot and achieve the desired voltage
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] levels.
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] Circuit Analysis
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] Your current circuit is essentially a voltage divider:
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 3.3V ──── R1 (trimpot) ────┬─── VIDEO OUT ──── 75Ω ──── GND
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat]                            │
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] GP28 ──── 330Ω ────────────┘
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] Desired Voltage Levels
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] For composite video:
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] - Black level (sync tip): 0.3V
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] - White level (peak): 0.77V (66% of 1V p-p above black)
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] Calculations
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] Let's define:
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] - R1 = resistor from 3.3V to output (replacing trimpot)
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] - R2 = 330Ω from GPIO to output
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] - R_load = 75Ω (TV input)
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 1. When GPIO outputs LOW (0V) - Black level
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] The circuit becomes:
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 3.3V ──── R1 ────┬─── VIDEO OUT (0.3V) ──── 75Ω ──── GND
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat]                  │
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat]                 330Ω
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat]                  │
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat]                 GND (GPIO = 0V)
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] Using voltage divider formula:
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 0.3V = 3.3V × (R_parallel / (R1 + R_parallel))
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] Where R_parallel = (330Ω × 75Ω) / (330Ω + 75Ω) = 61.11Ω
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] Solving for R1:
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 0.3 = 3.3 × (61.11 / (R1 + 61.11))
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] R1 = 3.3 × 61.11 / 0.3 - 61.11
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] R1 = 672.21 - 61.11 = 611.1Ω
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 2. When GPIO outputs HIGH (3.3V) - White level
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] The circuit becomes:
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 3.3V ──── R1 ────┬─── VIDEO OUT (0.77V) ──── 75Ω ──── GND
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat]                  │
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat]                 330Ω
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat]                  │
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat]                 3.3V (GPIO = 3.3V)
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] Now we have two voltage sources. Using superposition:
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] - From 3.3V through R1: contributes 0.3V (as calculated above)
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] - From GPIO through 330Ω: needs to add 0.47V (0.77V - 0.3V)
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] The contribution from GPIO:
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:05 [deepseek-chat] ΔV = 3.3V × (R_parallel2 / 330Ω)
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] Where R_parallel2 = (R1 × 75Ω) / (R1 + 75Ω)
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] We need ΔV = 0.47V:
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 0.47 = 3.3 × (R_parallel2 / 330)
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] R_parallel2 = (0.47 × 330) / 3.3 = 47Ω
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] Now solve for R1:
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 47 = (R1 × 75) / (R1 + 75)
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 47(R1 + 75) = 75R1
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 47R1 + 3525 = 75R1
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 3525 = 28R1
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] R1 = 125.89Ω
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] Solution
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] We have conflicting requirements:
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] - For black level (0.3V): R1 ≈ 611Ω
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] - For white level (0.77V): R1 ≈ 126Ω
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] This indicates the circuit needs adjustment. Let me suggest a better approach:
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] Recommended Circuit
2026-04-23 07:29:06 [deepseek-chat] 
