2026-04-23 08:08:52 [nitro@ryzen5] on rp2350 is gp28 best for digital out?
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] Excellent question! For the RP2350 (Raspberry Pi Pico 2), GPIO selection matters for high-speed
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] digital output like teletext.
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] RP2350 GPIO Analysis for Digital Output
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] GPIO28 Specifics:
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] - Bank: GPIO28 is in Bank 1 (GPIO24-29)
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] - SIO (Software I/O): Yes, all GPIOs support SIO
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] - PIO (Programmable I/O): Yes, all GPIOs can be used with PIO
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] - Drive Strength: Configurable (2mA, 4mA, 8mA, 12mA default)
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] - Slew Rate: Configurable (slow/fast)
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] Best GPIOs for High-Speed Digital Output:
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] • Top Tier (Fastest):*
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 1. GPIO0-7, GPIO16-23 - These are on the "QSPI" bank with potentially faster access
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 2. GPIO24-29 (including GPIO28) - Also good for high speed
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] • Why GPIO28 is Good:*
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] - Same performance as most other GPIOs for SIO use
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] - No special limitations
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] - Convenient location (near 3V3 and GND pins)
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] Potential Issues with GPIO28:
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 1. Shared Functions: GPIO28 can be used for ADC input (ADC2) - but this doesn't affect
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] digital output
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 2. No PIO State Machine Dedication: All GPIOs are equal for PIO
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] Even Better Options:
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] If you want maximum speed for teletext (6.9375 MHz):
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] • Option 1: Use PIO State Machine*
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] // Any GPIO can achieve ~125 MHz with PIO
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] // GPIO28 is perfectly fine for this
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] • Option 2: Use DMA + PWM for precise timing*
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] // GPIO28 works, but consider GPIO0-15 for simpler PWM mapping
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] • Option 3: Bit-banging with SIO*
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] // GPIO28 is fine, but GPIO0-7 might have slightly faster access
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] Performance Comparison
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] ╭──────────────────────┬────────────────────────┬──────────────────────╮
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] │  Method              │  Max Reliable Frequency │  Best GPIOs         │
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] │  SIO Bit-banging     │  ~10-15 MHz            │  GPIO0-7, GPIO16-23 │
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] │  PIO State Machine   │  ~62.5 MHz (sysclk/2)  │  ANY GPIO           │
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] │  PWM + DMA           │  ~62.5 MHz             │  GPIO0-15           │
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] │  SPI Hardware        │  ~62.5 MHz             │  GPIO16-19          │
2026-04-23 08:09:29 [deepseek-chat] ╰──────────────────────┴────────────────────────┴──────────────────────╯
