2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] For Your Teletext Application (6.9375 MHz):
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] GPIO28 is PERFECTLY ADEQUATE for:
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 1. PIO-based teletext generation (recommended)
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 2. SIO bit-banging (possible with careful coding)
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 3. PWM-based generation
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] But Consider These Alternatives:
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] • If using PIO (Best Approach):*
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] - GPIO28 is excellent
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] - Any GPIO works equally well with PIO
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] • If bit-banging with SIO:*
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] - GPIO0-7 might be 5-10% faster due to bus architecture
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] - Difference is negligible at 6.9375 MHz
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] • If space-constrained on PCB:*
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] - GPIO28's location near power pins is convenient
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] Recommendation
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] • Stick with GPIO28* because:
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 1. It's already in your design
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 2. Performance difference is negligible at 6.9375 MHz
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 3. All GPIOs have same drive strength/slew rate control
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 4. PIO can use any GPIO with identical performance
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] • To maximize performance with GPIO28:*
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] // Configure for maximum drive strength and fast slew
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] gpio_set_drive_strength(28, GPIO_DRIVE_STRENGTH_12MA);
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] gpio_set_slew_rate(28, GPIO_SLEW_RATE_FAST);
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] • If you want the absolute fastest option:*
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] - Use GPIO0 with PIO state machine
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] - But you'll gain maybe 1-2% at most
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] • Bottom line:* GPIO28 is perfectly suitable for teletext generation. The resistor network
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] design will have more impact on signal quality than GPIO selection.
2026-04-23 08:09:30 [deepseek-chat] 
