2026-04-23 08:12:56 [nitro@ryzen5] can i use a gpio for my 3.3V?
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] • No, you should NOT use a GPIO pin as a 3.3V power source* for your video circuit. Here's
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] why:
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] Critical Reasons NOT to Use GPIO for 3.3V:
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 1. Current Limitation
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - RP2350 GPIO pins: Max 12mA per pin (with 50mA total bank limit)
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - Your video circuit draws: 6-12mA continuous
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - This would:
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat]   - Push the GPIO near/at its maximum rating
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat]   - Cause voltage droop under load
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat]   - Risk damaging the microcontroller
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 2. Voltage Regulation
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - GPIO output voltage varies with load: ~3.0-3.3V under load
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - Video circuits need stable 3.3V for consistent black/white levels
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - GPIO pins have output impedance (~50Ω) causing voltage drop
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 3. Thermal Issues
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - Continuous 12mA through GPIO creates heat
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - No thermal protection on GPIO pins
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - Could damage the RP2350 over time
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 4. Noise and Stability
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - GPIO pins aren't designed as power supplies
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - Digital switching noise couples into your analog video signal
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] - Poor voltage regulation causes video level drift
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] What Happens If You Try:
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] GPIO as 3.3V ──── 470Ω ────┬─── VIDEO OUT ──── 75Ω ──── GND
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat]                            │
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] Data GPIO ─────── 150Ω ────┘
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:30 [deepseek-chat] • Problems:*
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 1. Voltage at VIDEO OUT becomes unpredictable
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 2. Data GPIO affects the "3.3V" supply level
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 3. Cross-coupling between data and supply
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 4. Possible latch-up or damage
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] Correct Solutions:
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] Option 1: Use Dedicated 3.3V Pin (Recommended)
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 3V3 pin ──── 470Ω ────┬─── VIDEO OUT ──── 75Ω ──── GND
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                       │
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] GPIO28 ───── 150Ω ────┘
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] Option 2: Use External 3.3V Regulator (Best for quality)
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] External 3.3V ──── 470Ω ────┬─── VIDEO OUT ──── 75Ω ──── GND
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                             │
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] GPIO28 ─────────── 150Ω ────┘
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] Option 3: Reconfigure Circuit (If you're out of 3.3V pins)
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] • Active Pull-up Circuit:*
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] GPIO28 (data) ──── 150Ω ────┬─── VIDEO OUT ──── 75Ω ──── GND
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                             │
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] GPIO29 (pull-up) ── 470Ω ───┘
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] - Use one GPIO for data, another for pull-up
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] - Still not ideal but better than single GPIO
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] Current Draw Calculations:
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] For 470Ω/150Ω circuit:
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] - When GPIO LOW: I = 3.3V / (470Ω + 75Ω||150Ω) ≈ 6.4mA
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] - When GPIO HIGH: I ≈ 3.2mA (current splits)
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] • This exceeds safe continuous GPIO current!*
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] The Right Way - Complete Circuit:
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] RP2350 3V3 pin ────────┬─────────────────────┐
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                        │                     │
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                     [470Ω]                 [0.1µF]
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                        │                     │
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] GPIO28 ─────────────[150Ω]───────────┬───────┘
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                                      │
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                                   VIDEO OUT ─────[75Ω]───── GND
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                                      │
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                                   [100pF] (optional for filtering)
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                                      │
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat]                                     GND
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] Summary:
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] • DO:*
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] - Use the dedicated 3V3(OUT) pin on RP2350
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] - This pin can supply 300mA+ (plenty for video)
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] - It's a regulated, clean 3.3V supply
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:31 [deepseek-chat] • DON'T:*
2026-04-23 08:13:32 [deepseek-chat] - Use any GPIO pin as a power supply
2026-04-23 08:13:32 [deepseek-chat] - Exceed GPIO current ratings (12mA/pin, 50mA/bank)
2026-04-23 08:13:32 [deepseek-chat] - Mix data and power on the same GPIO
2026-04-23 08:13:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:13:32 [deepseek-chat] • Your video quality will be much better with proper 3.3V from the power pin!*
2026-04-23 08:13:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:23:53 [nitro@ryzen5] should i consider anything on the gnd between pico 2 and rca
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] • Yes, ground considerations are CRITICAL for video quality!* Poor ground connections cause
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] several issues with composite video.
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] Common Ground Problems with Video:
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 1. Ground Loops - Hum bars (50/60Hz) rolling through picture
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 2. Impedance in Ground Path - Smearing, color bleeding, sync issues
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 3. Digital Noise Coupling - Sparkles, dots, interference patterns
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 4. DC Offset - Incorrect black/white levels
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] Your Specific Setup:
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] Pico 2 ────[Video Circuit]──── RCA ──── TV
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat]   GND                             GND
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] Critical Considerations:
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 1. Single Ground Point (Most Important!)
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] Pico 2 GND ──────┬───── Video Circuit GND
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat]                  │
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat]               [Direct, thick connection]
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat]                  │
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat]               RCA Shield ──── TV GND
2026-04-23 08:24:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] • DO NOT:* Create multiple ground paths or ground loops.
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 2. Ground Wire Impedance
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - Problem: Thin ground wires act as resistors at video frequencies
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - Solution: Use short, thick ground connections
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - Example: 0.1Ω in ground path causes 10mV offset with 100mA current
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 3. Digital vs Analog Ground Separation
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]               Pico 2
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]          ┌─────────────┐
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]          │ Digital     │
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]          │ Circuits    │
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]          │             │
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]          │  AGND───────┼───╮
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]          │   │         │   │
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]          │  DGND───────┼───┤
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]          └─────────────┘   │
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                            │
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                     [10Ω resistor] ← Star point
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                            │
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                     Video Circuit GND
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                            │
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                         RCA Shield
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 4. RCA Connector Grounding
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - RCA shield MUST connect directly to circuit ground
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - Use shielded cable with shield connected at both ends
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - Avoid ground loops through power supplies
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] Recommended Implementation:
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] Option A: Direct Connection (Simplest)
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] Pico 2 GND pin ────[Thick wire]─────┬───── Video Circuit GND
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                                     │
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                                  RCA Shield
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] Option B: Star Ground (Better)
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                     ┌───── Video Circuit
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] Pico 2 GND ──────★──┼───── RCA Shield
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]                     └───── Power Supply GND (if separate)
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] Option C: Isolated Ground (Best for noisy environments)
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] Pico 2 ──── Video Circuit ────[Isolation Transformer]─── RCA ──── TV
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat]   GND          GND                                           GND
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] Specific Issues to Watch For:
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 1. Hum Bars (50/60Hz)
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - Cause: Ground loop through power supplies
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - Fix: Use same power supply for Pico and TV, or add isolation
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 2. Sparkles/Dots
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - Cause: Digital noise coupling through shared ground
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] - Fix: Separate digital and analog grounds with ferrite bead
2026-04-23 08:24:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 3. Sync Problems
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] - Cause: Ground impedance causing timing errors
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] - Fix: Direct, low-impedance ground connection
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 4. Color Bleeding
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] - Cause: High-frequency ground impedance
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] - Fix: Ground plane or wide ground traces
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] Practical Implementation:
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] • On Breadboard:*
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] Pico 2 GND ────[Jumper wire]─── Video Circuit GND ──── RCA center pin
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat]                           │
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat]                        [0.1µF] to Pico GND (optional bypass)
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat]                           │
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat]                        RCA shield ──── TV GND
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] • On PCB:*
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] - Use ground plane under video circuit
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] - Keep video components close together
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] - Route ground first, then signals
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] Testing Procedure:
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 1. Check DC Resistance: GND to GND should be < 0.1Ω
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 2. Check AC Coupling: Add 0.1µF capacitor in series with RCA shield if hum persists
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 3. Oscilloscope Test: Look for noise on ground line at video output
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] Final Recommendation:
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] For your Pico 2 to RCA video connection:
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] • Do This:*
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 1. Connect Pico GND directly to video circuit GND with short, thick wire
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 2. Connect video circuit GND directly to RCA shield
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 3. Use single ground point - no loops
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 4. Keep digital circuits away from video ground path
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] • Avoid This:*
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 1. Multiple ground paths to TV
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 2. Long, thin ground wires
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 3. Ground connections through breadboard power rails (high impedance)
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 4. Mixing power supply grounds without isolation
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] • Simple Rule:* "One ground wire from Pico to video circuit to RCA shield, as short and
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] thick as possible."
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] • Would you like a complete schematic showing proper grounding?*
2026-04-23 08:24:32 [deepseek-chat] 
