2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] Key Differences for RP2040:
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 1. BOOTSEL Pin: On RP2040, the boot selection is typically GPIO 25 (shared with LED)
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 2. Hardware Registers: Use `gpio_*` functions instead of direct register manipulation
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 3. Pull Configuration: Need to explicitly set pull-up resistor
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 4. State Restoration: Must save/restore GPIO configuration
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] Alternative: Using the SDK's Built-in Function
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] If you're using the Pico SDK, there's already a function for this:
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] #include "pico/bootrom.h"
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] bool ReadBootSel() {
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat]     return rom_func_lookup_inline(ROM_FUNC_RESET_USB_BOOT) != NULL ?
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat]            rom_func_lookup_inline(ROM_FUNC_RESET_USB_BOOT)(0, 0) : false;
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] }
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] Or simpler:
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] bool ReadBootSel() {
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat]     // Check if BOOTSEL button is pressed on startup
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat]     // Note: This only works during the first few milliseconds after reset
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat]     return rom_func_lookup_inline(ROM_FUNC_RESET_USB_BOOT) != NULL;
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] }
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] Important Notes:
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 1. Timing: The BOOTSEL button is only sampled during the first few milliseconds after
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] power-on
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 2. GPIO 25: On Pico, GPIO 25 is shared with the LED - you may need to disable LED control
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 3. No Flash: The `noinlinenotinflash_func` macro ensures this runs
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] from RAM, not flash
2026-04-23 10:06:45 [deepseek-chat] 
