2026-04-23 10:21:50 [nitro@ryzen5] is this because it is analog pin also?
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] • YES! That's exactly it! GP28 on RP2040 is ADC2* - an analog input pin. When
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] configured as a digital INPUT, analog pins can behave differently.
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] The ADC Pin Quirk:
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] On RP2040, GPIO 26-29 are ADC inputs (ADC0-ADC3). When used as digital inputs:
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 1. They have different input characteristics than regular digital pins
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 2. The ADC multiplexer adds leakage/impedance
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 3. They may not achieve true high-Z in INPUT mode
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] Your GPIO28 (ADC2) Behavior:
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] When you set GP28 to `GPIO_IN`:
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] - It's not truly high impedance
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] - It has ~12.6Ω to ground (from your measurements)
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] - This is likely the ADC input impedance or ESD protection circuitry
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] Confirmation:
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] Check the RP2040 datasheet - ADC pins have:
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] - Input impedance: Typically 500Ω-1kΩ, but can be lower
2026-04-23 10:22:16 [deepseek-chat] - Leakage current: Higher than digital-only pins
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] - ESD diodes: Create a path to ground/VDD
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] Solutions:
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 1. Use a Different GPIO (Best Solution)
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] Use a digital-only pin instead of GP28:
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] - GPIO 0-25 are digital-only (except 23-25 have special functions)
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] - Try GPIO 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 - these are clean digital pins
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 2. Modify Circuit for ADC Pin
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] If you must use GP28, design for its ~12.6Ω input impedance:
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 3.3V ──── 68Ω ────┬─── VIDEO OUT ──── 75Ω ──── GND
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat]                   │
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] GP28 ──── 33Ω ────┘
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 3. Add External Pull-up (Hack)
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] Add a strong external pull-up when in INPUT mode:
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 3.3V ──── 220Ω ────┬─── VIDEO OUT ──── 75Ω ──── GND
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat]                    │
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] GP28 ──── 100Ω ────┘
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat]                    │
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat]                  1kΩ (external pull-up)
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat]                    │
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat]                  3.3V
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] Recommended Action:
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 10:22:17 [deepseek-chat] • Switch to GPIO0* (or any GPIO 0-22):
