2026-04-23 10:56:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] Using tristate GPIO pins is an excellent and hardware-efficient method for generating the
2026-04-23 10:56:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] intermediate voltage levels required for analog video. By switching a pin between High (driving
2026-04-23 10:56:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] VCC), Low (driving GND), and High-Impedance (input mode), you can effectively create a rudimentary
2026-04-23 10:56:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] Digital-to-Analog Converter (DAC) when combined with series resistors and the display's standard
2026-04-23 10:56:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] 75-ohm termination.
2026-04-23 10:56:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
