2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] Looking at the code, I can see the issue with adding a second row of WST teletext. The problem is
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] in the timing and buffer management. Here's what's happening:
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] The Issue:
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 1. Buffer Size: `wstWords = 333` (lines)
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 2. Current Usage:
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat]    - Even field: 12 blank lines + 1 header + 1 body + 295 blanks = 309 lines ✓
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat]    - Odd field: 12 blank lines + 1 header + 1 body + 296 blanks = 310 lines ✓
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 3. When adding a second row: You're trying to add more teletext packets, but the timing
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] calculations in the WST PIO program (`wst.pio`) and the DMA configuration aren't accounting for the
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] extra time needed.
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] The Root Cause:
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] The `wst.pio` program has a fixed timing structure:
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] - Waits for video IRQ
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] - Delays 20 cycles
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] - Transmits `x` bits (where `x` is from the FIFO)
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] When you add a second teletext row, you're adding 384 more bits (53.045 µs) of transmission time,
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] which extends beyond the expected line timing.
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] Solutions:
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] Option 1: Adjust Blank Line Count
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] Reduce the number of blank lines to compensate:
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] void initTeletext() {
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	int p = 0;
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	int skip1 = 12;
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	int skip2 = 294;  // Reduced by 1 to account for extra row
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	// Even field
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	for(int i=0; i<skip1; i++) wstEven[p++] = 0;
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	wstEven[p++] = 384;
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	wstHeader(1, 0, 0, title32, &wstEven[p]); p += 12;
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	wstEven[p++] = 384;
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	wstBody(1, 1, line40, &wstEven[p]); p += 12;
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	wstEven[p++] = 384;  // Second row
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	wstBody(1, 2, line40, &wstEven[p]); p += 12;  // Note: row 2
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	for(int i=0; i<skip2; i++) wstEven[p++] = 0;
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 	// Similar adjustment for odd field...
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] }
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] Option 2: Check WST PIO Timing
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] The `wst.pio` program might need adjustment. Currently it has:
2026-04-23 13:57:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] nop [20]  ; Fixed 20 cycle delay
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] This might need to be reduced or made variable based on content.
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] Option 3: Verify Video Sync
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] The video PIO (`vidblit.pio`) generates an IRQ at the end of each line. Make sure the WST PIO is
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] properly synchronized:
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] // In main loop, check both state machines
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] uint32_t video_stall = 1u << (PIO_FDEBUG_TXSTALL_LSB + VideoStateMachine);
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] uint32_t wst_stall = 1u << (PIO_FDEBUG_TXSTALL_LSB + TeletextStateMachine);
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] if ((pio0->fdebug & (video_stall | wst_stall)) != 0) {
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat]     // Handle stall condition
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat]     pio0->fdebug = video_stall | wst_stall;
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat]     led = !led;
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] }
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] Option 4: Adjust DMA Transfer Counts
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] When adding more teletext rows, update the DMA transfer counts:
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] void vid_field(int field) {
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 	if (field & 1) {
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 		dma_channel_set_trans_count(video_dma_chan, wordCount + words, false);
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 		dma_channel_set_read_addr(video_dma_chan, oddFrame, true);
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 		dma_channel_set_trans_count(wst_dma_chan, wstWords+1, false);  // +1 for odd field
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 		dma_channel_set_read_addr(wst_dma_chan, wstOdd, true);
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 	} else {
2026-04-23 13:57:20 [deepseek-chat] 		dma_channel_set_trans_count(video_dma_chan, wordCount, false);
