2026-04-23 16:30:09 [nitro@ryzen5] with rp2350 pio, how many loops does this code do
2026-04-23 16:30:11 [nitro@ryzen5] 	out	y,32vsync:		jmp	y--,vsync
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] It will loop \(2^{32}\) times.
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] Why: `out y, 32` loads all 32 shifted bits into `y`.
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] Then `jmp y--, vsync` is a post-decrement loop condition: it jumps while `y` was non-zero,
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] decrementing each time.
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] So if `y` starts at `0xFFFFFFFF`, you get exactly 4,294,967,295 jumps taken, plus one final
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] non-jump evaluation when `y` reaches zero.
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] People usually call that a 2^32-iteration delay loop.
2026-04-23 16:30:16 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:50 [nitro@ryzen5] it is what is in the fifo
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] [gpt-5.3-codex] Exactly — the loop count is determined by the FIFO word you pulled into `y` via:
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] `out y, 32`
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] Then:
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] `jmp y--, vsync`
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] behaves like:
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] - if `y != 0`: jump, then decrement `y`
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] - if `y == 0`: don’t jump, then wrap/decrement internally
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] So for an initial value `N` in `y`, the jump is taken N times (for `N` in 1…0xFFFFFFFF),
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] then falls through once.
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] Quick cases:
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `N = 0` → 0 loops (falls through immediately)
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `N = 1` → 1 loop
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `N = 1234` → 1234 loops
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `N = 0xFFFFFFFF` → 4,294,967,295 loops
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] So yes: it’s “whatever is in the FIFO” (interpreted as an unsigned 32-bit count).
2026-04-23 16:30:54 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
