2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here are a few observations and thoughts on the provided code:
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] • Hardware and Timing Design*
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] • System Clock: Setting the system clock to 166.5 MHz is a clever choice. It provides
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] exactly 10,656 cycles for a 64 µs PAL line, and perfectly divides by 24 to hit the exact 6.9375
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] Mbps data rate required for World System Teletext (WST).
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] • 3-Level Video DAC: Using the GPIO direction (`pindirs`) to toggle the pin between driven
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] low (Sync), high-impedance (Black level), and driven high (White level) alongside an external
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] resistor network is a highly efficient way to generate the composite signal without requiring an
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] external DAC or multiple pins.
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] • Code Structure and Logic*
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] • PIO Hardcoding: In `vidbit.cpp` within the `vidinit` function, `pio0` is hardcoded in
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] the `piosminit` call (`int pioStatus=piosm_init(pio0, sm, offset1, &config);`), even
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] though a `PIO pio` pointer is passed as an argument to the function. You might want to update this
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] to use the passed variable for consistency, should you ever move the video state machine to `pio1`
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] or `pio2`.
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] • Teletext Encoding: Your implementation of the Hamming 8/4 encoding and odd parity
2026-04-23 21:09:10 [gemini-3.1-pro] generation is clean and accurate. The 48-byte packet structure correctly accommodates the clock
2026-04-23 21:09:11 [gemini-3.1-pro] run-in, framing code, magazine/row, and the 40-byte payload.
2026-04-23 21:09:11 [gemini-3.1-pro] • DMA Pacing: Pacing the DMA transfers using the PIO TX FIFO (`DREQ`) is the ideal approach
2026-04-23 21:09:11 [gemini-3.1-pro] here, ensuring the C++ main loop is free to handle audio generation, PS/2 parsing, and field
2026-04-23 21:09:11 [gemini-3.1-pro] management without disrupting the strict video timing.
