2026-04-24 00:00:09 [nitro@ryzen5] there is still single videoStall being triggered, no code, just discussion. ideas?
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] Yes — a single early `videoStall` is usually startup phasing, not steady-state bandwidth.
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] Likely causes (in order):
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] - PIO enabled before first DMA transfer is armed/prefilled
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	SM starts consuming immediately; one underflow happens once, then system catches up.
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] - First field handoff race in main loop (`if !dma busy -> start`)
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	There can be a brief gap before first `vid_field()` fires.
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Teletext IRQ contention at line start during bring-up
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	Only enough to cause one hiccup at boot.
2026-04-24 00:00:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] - DMA channel cold-start latency (bus arbitration/cache effects)
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	One-time, then stable.
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] How to think-check without code:
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] - If it happens once after boot and never again: startup sequencing issue.
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] - If it happens at field boundaries repeatedly: rearm timing gap.
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] - If it correlates with WST enable: cross-load contention.
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] Practical strategy:
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] 1) Ensure first frame DMA is armed before enabling video SM.
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] 2) Optionally prefill TX FIFO before run.
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] 3) Clear/debug flags once after startup and ignore initial event if picture is stable.
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] Given your “single stall” symptom and good on-screen result, this strongly sounds like a harmless
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] first-frame underflow blip.
2026-04-24 00:00:19 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
