2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] From your PIO’s point of view, think in half-line slots (32 µs each), since the vertical
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] sequence is defined at half-line cadence.
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] For each field, vertical interval = 15 consecutive half-line slots:
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] - 5 × pre-equalizing
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] - 5 × broad/serration
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] - 5 × post-equalizing
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] Inside each 32 µs half-line slot:
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Equalizing slot: short sync pulse (about 2.35 µs low), rest high/blank.
2026-04-24 11:55:56 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Broad slot: long low pulse (about 27.3 µs low), but with short serration “high notches”
2026-04-24 11:55:57 [gpt-5.3-codex] at line-rate so H timing is still present.
