2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] Other things to account for:
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] 1) FIFO/DMA provisioning
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Must guarantee all 40 words are available before/through VSYNC sequence.
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] - If TX underflows once, timing is broken for that field.
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] 2) Cycle accounting
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Your low/high loop counts must include instruction overhead (set/out/jmp path cost), not just raw
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] desired microseconds.
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] 3) Field phasing
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Odd/even still need correct half-line phase relationship for true interlace.
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] 4) Line budget continuity
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Total time consumed by new VSYNC sequence must match your frame timing budget so active raster
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] still starts where expected.
2026-04-24 12:17:07 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 12:17:08 [gpt-5.3-codex] 5) WST timing reference shift
2026-04-24 12:17:08 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Since you currently key WST timing off video behavior, changing VSYNC structure may shift your
