2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] Your codebase shows a solid understanding of the RP2350’s PIO and DMA for generating PAL video.
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] I’ve reviewed the files and spotted a few issues that would likely prevent proper video output in
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] the current state. Below are my observations and suggestions.
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 1. DMA never started – likely cause of black/stalled output
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] - In `vidfield()` you reconfigure the DMA transfer but never call `dmachannel_start()`.
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Because the initial `dmachannelconfigure()` in `viddmainit()` uses `false` (don’t
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] start), the DMA remains idle and the PIO will stall waiting for data.
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Fix: Add `dmachannelstart(videodmachan);` inside `vid_field()`, or start
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] the DMA once after the first field setup and rely on subsequent reconfigurations while it’s still
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] running (if you use a chaining scheme).
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 2. Mismatch between `vidblit.pio` and the frame buffer layout
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] - The PIO program in `vidblit.pio` contains two vertical‑sync generation blocks. The first
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] block (the one with `out pindirs, 1` and `out y, 31`) will consume 41 words before the
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] second block, making the total FIFO read‑out 83 words prior to the line loop.
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Your C code only supplies 42 preamble words (according to the comments, word 0 =
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] interlace delay, words 1‑40 = vsync counts, 41 = linecounter, 42 = pixelcounter).
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro]   The first block therefore reads data meant for the second block, leading to a FIFO underflow and
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] persistent stall.
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Recommendation: Remove the first vsync block from the PIO file (keep only the second one
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] with `set pindirs, 1` / `out y, 32`) so that the consumption matches the comment and your frame
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] buffer.
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 3. Hardcoded `pio0` in `vidinit()` (and similarly in `wstinit()`)
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] int pioStatus = pio_sm_init(pio0, sm, offset1, &config);   // uses pio0, not pio
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] The function receives a `PIO pio` argument but ignores it. If you ever change the PIO instance
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] (e.g., move video to `pio1`), this would still write to `pio0`.
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Fix: Use the parameter: `piosminit(pio, sm, offset1, &config);`
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 4. Audio sample generation never updates `pcm32`
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] In the `#ifdef STREAM_AUDIO` block:
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] int static16 = fuzz16() >> 5;
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] uint32_t pcm = ((static16 << 16) | ((pcm32 & 0xffff) >> 6));
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] pio_sm_put(pio1, AudioStateMachine, pcm);
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] `pcm32` is never modified, so the lower 16 bits stay zero and the audio becomes a constant‑biased
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] noise.
2026-04-24 15:43:26 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Fix: After computing `pcm`, set `pcm32 = pcm;` (or better, maintain a proper circular
2026-04-24 15:43:27 [deepseek-v4-pro] buffer for previous samples).
2026-04-24 15:43:27 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-24 15:43:27 [deepseek-v4-pro] 5. Other minor points
2026-04-24 15:43:27 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Field counter overflow: `int field` is incremented forever. Signed integer overflow is
2026-04-24 15:43:27 [deepseek-v4-pro] undefined behavior. Use `unsigned int` or wrap manually.
2026-04-24 15:43:27 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Teletext WST lines: The teletext generation logic looks correct for the given `wstWords`
