2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] Broad-sync with serration (PAL/625) is the middle part of vertical sync:
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] - It lasts 5 half-lines total.
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] - The signal is mostly at sync level (“broad” low interval),
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] - but every half-line includes a short opposite-level notch (the serration), timed at
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] line-rate spacing.
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] Why serrations exist:
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] - They keep horizontal timing separators/PLLs locked during vertical sync, since otherwise the long
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] broad sync could lose line-rate reference.
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-24 16:52:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] Practical half-line view (with your polarity `1 = sync`, `0 = black/float`):
