2026-04-24 17:22:01 [nitro@ryzen5] can you help fix my video signal generator, i am trying to add broadcast legal insterlace vertical blanking
2026-04-24 17:39:38 [kimi-k2.6] Your PIO blitter is clever—using the pin direction as a 1-bit DAC and front-loading the equalising
2026-04-24 17:39:38 [kimi-k2.6] / broad-sync pulses is a neat way to keep the line loop tight.  The main thing keeping it from
2026-04-24 17:39:38 [kimi-k2.6] being broadcast-legal is simply that the field lengths are wrong: `evenLines=309` and
2026-04-24 17:39:38 [kimi-k2.6] `oddLines=310` gives 619 total lines instead of 625, so the frame rate is about 24.6 Hz and the
2026-04-24 17:39:38 [kimi-k2.6] raster will roll or fail genlock.
2026-04-24 17:39:38 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] Because the PIO line loop is fixed at exactly one 64 µs line, and your odd/even preambles differ by
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] one half-line (16 vs 17 half-line periods), you cannot hit exactly 625.0 lines with integer line
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] counts.  The closest possible with this architecture is 305 / 304 full lines:
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] ╭─────────┬─────────────────────────┬──────────────┬────────────────────┬──────────────╮
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] │  Field  │  Preamble (half-lines)  │  Full lines  │  Equivalent lines  │  Field time  │
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] ├─────────┼─────────────────────────┼──────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────────┤
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] │  Even   │  16 (8 lines)           │  305         │  313               │  ~20.00 ms   │
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] │  Odd    │  17 (8.5 lines)         │  304         │  312.5             │  ~19.97 ms   │
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] ╰─────────┴─────────────────────────┴──────────────┴────────────────────┴──────────────╯
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] Total frame ≈ 39.97 ms (~25.02 Hz).  That is stable enough for almost any TV or capture
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] card, but be aware it is not sample-accurate broadcast 50 Hz—for strictly legal PAL you would need
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] the line loop to emit a half-line blanking period so both fields can be exactly 312.5 lines.
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] Below are the changes to add proper blanking and fix the timing.
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 1. `monobit.h`
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] Bump the line counts and add a blanking constant so the drawing routines know where active video
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] starts.
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] #pragma once
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] #include <stdint.h>
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] const int preamble = 34;
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] const int words = 27;
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] const int width = 864;
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] // 305/304 gives ~625.5 total line equivalents, the nearest we can get with
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] // integer full lines and 16/17 half-line preambles.
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] const int evenLines = 305;
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] const int oddLines = 304;
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] const int evenWords = preamble + evenLines * words;
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] const int oddWords = preamble + oddLines * words;
2026-04-24 17:39:39 [kimi-k2.6] 
