2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] What this fixes
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] 1. Correct line count – 305 / 304 gets the frame rate to within 0.1 % of 25 Hz.
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] 2. Black vertical blanking – all non-active lines are `0`, so the video DAC stays at black
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] level during the VBI.
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] 3. Interlace phase – the odd field still carries the extra `SYNC+E0,E1` half-line pulse, so
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] the two fields remain correctly interleaved.
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] If you later need exact broadcast 50 Hz
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] 
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] You will need to modify `vidblit.pio` so that one field can emit a trailing half-line blanking
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] period (or turn the line loop into a command stream that supports half-lines).  With the current
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] fixed 64 µs loop, one field will always be ≈ 32 µs shorter or longer than the other.  For now, the
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] 305/304 split is the nearest approximation.
2026-04-24 17:39:41 [kimi-k2.6] 
