2026-04-25 09:46:27 [nitro@ryzen5] describe PAL video spec signal for vertical blank period
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] In PAL composite video (625/50 system, often called PAL‑B/G/I), the vertical blanking
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] period (VBI) is the part of each field where active picture is suppressed so the display can
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] retrace from bottom to top.
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] Key PAL timing context
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Field rate: 50 fields/s (interlaced)
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Frame rate: 25 frames/s
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Line rate: 15.625 kHz
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Total lines: 625 per frame (312.5 per field)
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Line period (H): 64 µs
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] What happens during vertical blanking
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] During VBI, the waveform is not picture content; it contains:
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 1. Pre‑equalizing pulses
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 2. Vertical sync serration pulses
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 3. Post‑equalizing pulses
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 4. Remaining blanked lines (with normal line sync structure, no active video)
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] These pulses keep horizontal and vertical sync locked and preserve interlace (half‑line offset
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] between odd/even fields).
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] Pulse structure (PAL 625/50)
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] Around the field transition, PAL uses the classic CCIR/ITU equalizing + serration sequence:
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Equalizing pulses: short pulses at 2H rate (one every 32 µs), nominal pulse width
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] about 2.35 µs
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Vertical serration pulses: broader sync pulses aligned with line timing, nominal low
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] interval about 27.3 µs within each 32 µs half‑line segment
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Sequence is typically:
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	- 5 pre‑equalizing pulses
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	- 5 serration pulses
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	- 5 post‑equalizing pulses
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] This occupies about 2.5 lines before and 2.5 lines after the vertical sync center
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] (total ~5 lines of equalizing/serration structure).
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] Amplitude levels (composite video, 75 Ω)
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] Using the standard 1 Vp‑p composite scale:
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Sync tip: 0 V (most negative level)
2026-04-25 09:46:41 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Blanking level: 0.3 V
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Peak white: 1.0 V
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] So sync amplitude is 300 mV below blanking.
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] (If expressed in IRE: PAL typically uses 0 IRE for black at blanking, unlike NTSC setup variants.)
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] Lines in VBI
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] In 625‑line PAL, each field has roughly:
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] - ~17.5 lines vertical blanking
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] - ~295 active lines
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] (total 312.5 lines/field)
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] Exact line numbering/use depends on standardization context (broadcast, teletext, VITC, WSS, test
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] signals, etc.), but active picture generally begins after the vertical sync/equalizing interval and
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] associated blanked lines.
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] Practical note
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] The PAL VBI often carries ancillary data on specific lines (e.g., teletext, WSS,
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] VPS, VITC), while lines reserved for switching/equalizing remain non‑picture timing
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] content.
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] If you want, I can also give you a line-by-line map (field 1/field 2) for PAL‑B/G showing
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] where sync, blanking, and common data services are placed.
2026-04-25 09:46:42 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
