2026-04-25 09:56:19 [nitro@ryzen5] i want to know about half lines
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] [gpt-5.3-codex] Perfect — half-lines are the key to interlace in PAL.
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] PAL half-line concept (625/50)
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] A full line is 64 µs.
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] A half-line is 32 µs.
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] Because PAL is interlaced:
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] - each field is 312.5 lines
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] - that “.5” is literally one half-line offset between fields
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] That offset makes field 2 land between field 1 lines, giving true 2:1 interlace.
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] Where half-lines appear
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] They appear in the vertical sync interval, via equalizing and serration pulses spaced at
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] half-line timing (32 µs cadence), and at the field boundary (start/end) so one field is
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] shifted by half a line.
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] Why equalizing pulses are at 2H rate
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] Normal horizontal sync repeats every 64 µs (H).
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] During vertical sync, PAL inserts short pulses every 32 µs (H/2) so both line and field
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] timing stay locked and interlace phase is preserved.
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] Intuition
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] - If both fields started on whole-line boundaries, lines would stack on top of each other
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] (progressive-like sampling).
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] - The half-line shift forces alternate fields to be vertically staggered.
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] Practical timing view
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] One field duration:
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] - 312.5 × 64 µs = 20 ms
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] Two fields:
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] - 40 ms (25 frames/s)
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] So the half-line is not an oddity — it is structurally required to hit 50 fields/s with 625
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] interlaced lines.
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] If you want, I can draw a compact text timing diagram showing pre-eq → serration → post-eq
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] on a half-line grid.
2026-04-25 09:56:28 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
