2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] I’ll use:
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] - H = 64 µs
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] - H/2 = 32 µs
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `E` = equalizing pulse (short, ~2.35 µs)
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `S` = serration pulse (broad vertical-sync portion, ~27.3 µs low in each half-line slot)
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] 1) Vertical sync pulse train on half-line slots
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] Around field sync, the classic pattern is:
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] `E E E E E  S S S S S  E E E E E`
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] That is:
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] - 5 pre-equalizing pulses
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] - 5 serration pulses
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] - 5 post-equalizing pulses
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] Each symbol sits one half-line (32 µs) apart.
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] So total span is:
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] - 15 half-lines = 7.5 lines = 480 µs
2026-04-25 09:57:50 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
