2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] In your PIO pulse loop, each pulse has overhead:
2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `out y, 31` = 1 cycle
2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `out pindirs, 1` = 1 cycle
2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `jmp x--, pulse` = 1 cycle
2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] - plus the `jmp y--, phase` loop itself (`y+1` cycles total)
2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] So per pulse segment, elapsed cycles are:
2026-04-26 14:46:21 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 14:46:22 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `value + 3` (because the delay loop gives `value` cycles, then +3 housekeeping)
2026-04-26 14:46:22 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 14:46:22 [gpt-5.3-codex] Therefore each half-line pair is:
2026-04-26 14:46:22 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 14:46:22 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `(E0+3) + (E1+3) = 5322 + 6 = 5328`
2026-04-26 14:46:22 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `(B0+3) + (B1+3) = 5322 + 6 = 5328`
2026-04-26 14:46:22 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `(S0+3) + (S1+3) = 5320 + 6 = 5326`
2026-04-26 14:46:22 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
