2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] In practice:
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Integer-friendly PLL settings usually behave cleaner.
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Fractional divider involvement can introduce periodic phase error (tiny, but measurable
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] in tight timing work).
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Peripherals/state machines clocked from differently divided domains can show beat patterns
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] depending on ratios.
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] If you want the cleanest deterministic timing on RP2350, prefer clock plans with simple integer
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] ratios end-to-end (PLL → sys_clk → peripheral clock), and avoid fractional steps where possible.
2026-04-26 15:36:53 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
