2026-04-26 15:54:45 [gpt-5.3-codex] very similar. But they are not guaranteed equal jitter-wise just because they’re
2026-04-26 15:54:45 [gpt-5.3-codex] XOSC-derived.
2026-04-26 15:54:45 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 15:54:45 [gpt-5.3-codex] What changes jitter in practice:
2026-04-26 15:54:45 [gpt-5.3-codex] - PLL operating point (VCO frequency, loop behavior)
2026-04-26 15:54:45 [gpt-5.3-codex] - divider choices and where division happens
2026-04-26 15:54:45 [gpt-5.3-codex] - clock-tree coupling/noise at that system frequency
2026-04-26 15:54:45 [gpt-5.3-codex] - supply/board noise sensitivity at that frequency
2026-04-26 15:54:46 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-26 15:54:46 [gpt-5.3-codex] So: same XOSC lineage ≠ same final jitter.
2026-04-26 15:54:46 [gpt-5.3-codex] You need the specific PLL configuration to compare meaningfully.
