2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] For composite video level setting, resistor ratio accuracy matters.
2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] Benefits over 5% carbon film:
2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] - More accurate sync/blank/white amplitudes
2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Better channel-to-channel consistency (if you build more than one)
2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Lower temp drift and noise (small but real)
2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] Will it alone fix shimmer? Usually not. Shimmer is more often timing/edge/grounding
2026-04-27 10:53:18 [gpt-5.3-codex] related. But 1% resistors help get stable, correct levels and reduce one source of variation.
