2026-04-27 12:00:08 [nitro@ryzen5] can i design real keyboard with cheap good quality caps?
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] Yes — absolutely.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] If you mean a real custom keyboard, you can keep it low-cost and still good quality.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] Practical low-cost keyboard choices
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 1. MX-compatible mechanical switches (most common)
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Best balance of cost, feel, repairability.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Use hot-swap sockets if you want easy switch changes.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 2. Keycaps
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Cheapest decent: ABS doubleshot.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Better long-term: PBT dye-sub (usually pricier).
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 3. Stabilizers (for long keys)
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Use plate-mount or screw-in depending on case/plate.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Even cheap stabs can feel good if lubed/tuned.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] Electronics (important for reliability)
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Matrix + diodes (1 per key, e.g. 1N4148).
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - ESD protection on external connector if detachable keyboard.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Decoupling:
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	- 100 nF near controller
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	- 10 µF bulk nearby
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] About “cheap good quality caps”
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] Yes:
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Use X7R ceramic for 100 nF decouplers.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Use electrolytic/polymer for bulk (10–47 µF).
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Avoid relying on Y5U/Z5U for critical timing/filtering.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] So: cheap is fine, just pick the right dielectric/type.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] If you want, I can suggest a minimal 8x8 matrix schematic and parts list tuned for your
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] RP2350 system.
2026-04-27 12:00:15 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
