2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] What’s Notable or Novel
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] - 166.5 MHz system clock – Higher than the usual 150 MHz, giving 10 cycles per pixel and
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] cleaner division into the 10656-cycle PAL line.
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Teletext (WST) via a second PIO – Very unusual in hobbyist projects; the Hamming‑8/4
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] encoding and packet formatting are correctly implemented.
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] - Unified approach – One RP2350 handles composite video, teletext, stereo audio, and a PS/2
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] keyboard, all using PIO+DMA without CPU intervention during active lines.
