2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] Code Review & Potential Issues
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] 1. Teletext IRQ Missing (`wst.pio` never triggered)
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] In `vidbit.pio`, the instruction `irq set 0` is commented out inside the back‑porch area.
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] `wst.pio` begins with `wait 1 irq 0` – it will never start unless you uncomment that `irq
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] set 0` (or use a side‑set pin to trigger it). This means the teletext feature is currently
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] non‑functional.
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] • Fix:* Uncomment the `irq set 0` after the back‑porch delay, e.g.:
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] set pindirs, 0
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] set pins, 1
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] irq set 0            ; signal teletext SM
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] 2. H‑Sync Timing Mismatch (`vidbit.pio`)
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] The comment claims `27*29+3 = 786` cycles for h‑sync, but the loop actually runs:
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] set pins, 0        ; 1
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] set pindirs, 1     ; 1
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] set y, 26         ; 1
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] hsync loop:        ; 26×29 + 1 = 755
2026-04-29 11:22:37 [deepseek-v4-pro] ------------------
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] Total: 758 cycles
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] That’s 28 cycles short of the intended 786. PAL tolerates small errors, but the h‑sync pulse width
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] might be slightly out of spec.
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] • Suggestion:* Adjust the initial `set y, 27` and/or the delay value to match the comments,
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] or recalculate the comment to reflect actual cycles.
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 3. Floating Point in Initialization (`monobit.cpp`)
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] `sinf` is used inside a double loop. While it only runs once at startup, it requires linking with
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] the math library (`-lm`) and may pull in floating‑point code that could conflict with other
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] timing‑critical code. If ROM space is tight, consider a fixed‑point sine approximation or a
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] pre‑computed table.
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 4. DMA Field Queuing (`vidbit.cpp`)
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] The main loop starts the next field’s DMA as soon as the current one finishes. If the PIO hasn’t
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] drained its TX FIFO before the new DMA begins, you could get a glitch.
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] • Safer approach:* Use a double‑buffer vs. line‑by‑line DMA, or at minimum ensure the FIFO
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] is empty by checking `piosmistxfifo_empty()` before re‑arming the DMA.
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 5. LED Indicator on Stall Flags
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] The code clears the stall flags after detecting them:
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] if (pio0->fdebug & videoStall) {
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro]     pio0->fdebug = videoStall;
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro]     led = !led;
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] }
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] This is a clever way to monitor PIO FIFO underruns, but clearing the flag after reading can
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] cause flicker of the LED. Consider toggling `led` only when a real underrun condition is detected
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] (e.g., counting occurrences).
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 6. Possible Buffer Overlap in Bitmap Drawing
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] In `drawC64Char`, when `shift1 > 24`, two 32‑bit words are written horizontally. The `frame`
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] pointer is `(y>>1)*lineWords + offset`. This works, but ensure `lineWords` is correctly sized for
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] the maximum pixel column (`lineWidth-1`).
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] Minor Improvements
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] 
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] - C vs. C++ – The `monobit.cpp` header includes `<math.h>` (C style) but the code uses C++
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] (`while(char c=*text++)`). It’s fine, but consider using `extern "C"` if mixing with plain C
2026-04-29 11:22:38 [deepseek-v4-pro] elsewhere.
