2026-04-29 17:07:50 [scudmarks@discord] are you sure?
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] Yes, I’m sure. The Discord API exposes a user’s custom status through the `Presence` object.
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] Specifically:
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] - The custom status is stored as an activity with `type: 4` (CUSTOM_STATUS).
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] - The text is in the `state` field of that activity.
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] To access it, your bot needs:
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] 1. The privileged `GatewayIntentBits.GuildPresences` intent (must be enabled in the Discord
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] Developer Portal).
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] 2. The bot must be in the same guild as the user.
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] 3. When fetching a member, you need to ensure presence data is included – e.g. `await
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] guild.members.fetch({ user: authorId, force: true })` or by enabling the intent and relying on
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] gateway events.
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] Here’s a concrete example adapted for your `sloppybot.ts`:
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4] discordClient.on('messageCreate', async (message) => {
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4]   if (message.author.bot) return;
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4]   // Fetch member with presence
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4]   const member = await message.guild.members.fetch({ user: message.author.id, force: true });
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4]   const customStatus = member.presence?.activities?.find(a => a.type === 4)?.state;
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4]   if (customStatus) {
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4]     console.log(`[CUSTOM STATUS] ${message.author.tag}: ${customStatus}`);
2026-04-29 17:08:02 [deepseek-v4]   }
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] });
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] If the intent is not enabled, `member.presence` will be `null`.
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] So yes – you can grab the user’s “thinking” text (custom status) from a Discord bot, as
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] long as you have the right permissions. There’s no separate “thinking” field in the Discord API;
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] it’s exactly the custom status.
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] If you need help adding the intent to your sloppybot code, let me know.
2026-04-29 17:08:03 [deepseek-v4] 
