2026-04-29 17:23:35 [deepseek-v4] - The PAL timing constants and line structure look correct for 576i at 166.5 MHz.
2026-04-29 17:23:35 [deepseek-v4] - `drawC64Char` handles the 8‑pixel glyph spanning two 32‑bit words when `shift1 > 24` — that’s
2026-04-29 17:23:35 [deepseek-v4] good.
2026-04-29 17:23:35 [deepseek-v4] - In `rect`, the mask calculation for the right edge may produce unexpected results when `shift` is
2026-04-29 17:23:35 [deepseek-v4] negative (i.e. when `xoff + w > 32`). The `if(shift>0)` guard prevents that case, but then the full
2026-04-29 17:23:35 [deepseek-v4] 32‑bit word is used and the width loop continues to the next word — seems fine.
2026-04-29 17:23:35 [deepseek-v4] - `initFrame()` writes `statusText` at y‑coordinate `288*2 = 576`, which is beyond the visible area
2026-04-29 17:23:35 [deepseek-v4] for PAL 576i (576 lines total, but active area is smaller). Might be intentional for overscan.
