2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] General Structure
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] Your `Slop Fountain` is a sophisticated multi-model research tool. The architecture uses a relay
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] pattern to route messages through various LLM endpoints, with a custom raw-mode prompt
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] (`slopprompt.ts`) supporting grapheme clusters and terminal width calculations. The C++ `vidbit`
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] and `monobit` modules generate PAL 576i video on an RP2350, while the `wst.pio` program formats
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] World System Teletext packets.
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] Noteworthy Details
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 1. `slopfountain.ts`: The `relay()` function handles both legacy chat completions and the
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] newer `responses` endpoint (used by GPT‑5.3‑codex). However, the two paths are implemented in a
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] single large function which makes it harder to maintain. Extracting the responses‑specific logic
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] into its own helper could improve clarity.
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 2. `slopprompt.ts`: Your grapheme segmentation and terminal width calculation are robust.
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] However, the note about possible corruption when a multi‑byte UTF‑8 sequence is split across
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] `reader.read()` calls is a real concern. Buffering incomplete sequences between reads would
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] eliminate this.
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 3. `monobit.cpp`: The `flipBits` function manually reverses bits. A small lookup table for
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 256 entries would be faster and simpler:
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4]    static const uint8_t BitReverse[256] = { /* precompute */ };
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4]    int flipBits(int b) { return BitReverse[b & 0xff]; }
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4]    (I'll only show this if requested.)
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 4. `vidbit.pio`: The PIO program uses tight jmp loops for timing. The line `set pins, 0`
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] before hsync is correct but lacks a leading edge pulse; PAL requires a 2.35 µs front porch before
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] sync. You might want to verify the exact timing against PAL‑B specification.
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 5. `accounts.json`: Good practice to store only metadata here and keep actual keys in
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] environment variables. The `disabled` field for NVIDIA and Alibaba is a nice touch.
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] 6. `sloppybot.ts`: It uses `Deno.connect` to port 8081 and sets `setNoDelay(true)` on a
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] `TcpConn`. However, the type cast to `TcpConn` is not always safe if the connection is not a TCP
2026-04-29 17:51:05 [deepseek-v4] socket (e.g., if it falls back to a Unix socket). Ensure you are connecting to a TCP listener.
2026-04-29 17:51:06 [deepseek-v4] 
