2026-04-30 12:54:06 [deepseek-v4] Important caveats
2026-04-30 12:54:06 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 12:54:06 [deepseek-v4] - ICMP may be deprioritized – some routers treat ICMP Echo Requests as low priority, so
2026-04-30 12:54:06 [deepseek-v4] `mtr` results might not reflect real traffic (TCP/UDP) performance.
2026-04-30 12:54:06 [deepseek-v4] - True bottleneck detection often requires measuring throughput (bandwidth), not
2026-04-30 12:54:06 [deepseek-v4] just latency. For that, use iperf3 (test TCP/UDP throughput between two endpoints).
2026-04-30 12:54:06 [deepseek-v4] - If you are only interested in end‑to‑end latency and packet loss without hop‑by‑hop
2026-04-30 12:54:06 [deepseek-v4] details, standard `ping -c 100 <host>` (with 100 packets) gives a good baseline, but reveals no
2026-04-30 12:54:06 [deepseek-v4] where the issue lies.
