2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] 1. No actual packet loss end-to-end
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4]    Despite the 82% loss at hop 3 and the silent hops 8–12, the final destination has 0%
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] loss. This is normal: many routers deprioritise or rate‑limit ICMP Echo Requests (the packets
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] `mtr` uses). The data path (TCP for your rsync) likely suffers zero loss because real
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] traffic uses a different forwarding priority.
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4]    Conclusion: The 82% loss at hop 3 is not a bottleneck for your rsync sessions.
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] It is a cosmetic artifact of ICMP handling.
