2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] 3. Potential bandwidth bottleneck
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4]    `mtr` does not measure bandwidth. With 122 ms RTT and a typical TCP window size of 64 KB
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] (default on many systems), the maximum theoretical throughput is roughly:
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4]    Throughput ≈ TCP window size / RTT = 64 KB / 0.122 s ≈ 525 KB/s
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4]    This is far below what your link may support. If you are seeing slow rsync speeds, the primary
2026-04-30 12:57:12 [deepseek-v4] bottleneck is likely TCP window scaling and latency, not packet loss.
