2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] On Arch Linux, the file `/etc/sysctl.conf` does not exist by default. Instead, you place custom
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] sysctl snippets in `/etc/sysctl.d/`. On Alibaba Cloud (the destination), you already have a
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] `sysctl.conf` but it lacks TCP buffer tuning.
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] Here are the steps to apply TCP buffer adjustments on both your Arch machine and the
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] Alibaba server.
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 1. On your Arch Linux machine
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] Create a configuration file:
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/99-tcp-buffers.conf << 'EOF'
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] net.core.rmem_max = 134217728
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] net.core.wmem_max = 134217728
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] net.ipv4.tcp_rmem = 4096 87380 134217728
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] net.ipv4.tcp_wmem = 4096 65536 134217728
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] EOF
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] Apply it immediately:
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] sudo sysctl --system
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] (Alternatively, use `sudo sysctl -p /etc/sysctl.d/99-tcp-buffers.conf` if your version lacks
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] `--system`.)
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-04-30 13:01:10 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 2. On the Alibaba ECS (destination)
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] Append the same buffer settings to `/etc/sysctl.conf` or create a separate file under
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] `/etc/sysctl.d/`. I recommend appending to the existing file to keep all settings together:
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] cat >> /etc/sysctl.conf << 'EOF'
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] # TCP buffer tuning for high-latency links
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] net.core.rmem_max = 134217728
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] net.core.wmem_max = 134217728
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] net.ipv4.tcp_rmem = 4096 87380 134217728
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] net.ipv4.tcp_wmem = 4096 65536 134217728
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] EOF
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] Apply the changes:
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] sysctl -p
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] • (If `sysctl -p` gives an error about duplicate keys, check that `rp_filter` lines were not
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] duplicated – it is harmless.)*
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 3. Adjust your rsync command
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] Now use rsync with compression and larger socket buffers:
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] rsync -az --progress \
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4]       --sockopts="SO_RCVBUF=134217728,SO_SNDBUF=134217728" \
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4]       /path/to/source/ user@43.106.16.226:/path/to/destination/
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] • Explanation of the changes*
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] - `net.core.rmemmax / wmemmax` – absolute maximum TCP receive/send buffer size (128 MB).
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] - `tcprmem / tcpwmem` – sets the initial, default, and maximum buffer sizes. On a 122 ms
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] link, this allows TCP to scale its window up to ~128 MB, giving a theoretical throughput of `128 MB
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] / 0.122 s ≈ 1 GB/s` (though other factors cap it lower).
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] - The `--sockopts` option forces rsync itself to request the larger buffer.
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 4. Verify the buffers took effect
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] While an rsync is running, you can check the actual send/receive buffer sizes of the TCP
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] connection:
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] ss -ti | grep -A1 "rsync" | grep "skmem"
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] Look for `skmem:(r0,rb<value>,t0,tb<value>,...)` – the `rb` and `tb` values should be in the
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] megabyte range.
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-04-30 13:01:11 [deepseek-v4] 
