2026-05-01 13:42:51 [nitro@ryzen5] what is process with running two bots on discord using separate applications but same account
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] Here's a clear breakdown of how to run two separate Discord bots that belong to the
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] same Discord user account but use separate applications:
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 1. How Discord Handles This
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] - Each bot lives inside its own Application in the [Discord Developer
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications).
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] - One Discord user account can own multiple applications (and therefore multiple bots).
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] - Each application has its own Bot token.
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] - You cannot run two bots using the same token at the same time (Discord will disconnect
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] one of them).
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] So the normal and correct way is:
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 	One Discord account → Multiple Applications → Multiple Bots* (each with its own token)
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 2. Setup Process
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 1. Create two separate applications
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3]    - Go to the Developer Portal
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3]    - Create Application #1 → Enable the Bot
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3]    - Create Application #2 → Enable the Bot
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3]    - Generate a Bot Token for each one
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 2. Invite both bots to your server
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3]    - Each bot needs its own invite link (with the correct permissions).
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3]    - You can invite both bots to the same server.
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3] 3. Run them separately
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3]    - Each bot should run in its own process (or container).
2026-05-01 13:43:09 [grok-4.3]    - They should each load their own token from environment variables or config files.
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 3. Recommended Project Structure
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] project/
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] ├── bot1/
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │   ├── .env          # BOT1_TOKEN=...
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │   └── index.ts
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] ├── bot2/
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │   ├── .env          # BOT2_TOKEN=...
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │   └── index.ts
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] └── package.json
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] Or if you're using the same codebase for both:
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] // bot.ts
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] const token = Deno.env.get("DISCORD_TOKEN");
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] if (!token) throw new Error("Missing DISCORD_TOKEN");
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] // ... rest of your bot code
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] Then run them like this:
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] # Terminal 1
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] DISCORD_TOKEN=bot1_token deno run -A bot.ts
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] # Terminal 2
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] DISCORD_TOKEN=bot2_token deno run -A bot.ts
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 4. Important Notes
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] ╭───────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │  Question                                 │  Answer                              │
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] ├───────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │  Can two bots use the same token?         │  No                                  │
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │  Can one user own multiple bots?          │  Yes                                 │
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │  Do they need separate applications?      │  Yes                                 │
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │  Can they be in the same Discord server?  │  Yes                                 │
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │  Do they share rate limits?               │  No (each token has its own limits)  │
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] │  Can they talk to each other?             │  Yes, just like any other bots       │
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] ╰───────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 5. Common Use Cases
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] - Running two different models/personalities as bots
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] - One bot for public use, one for testing
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] - One bot per server with different configurations
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] - Running the same code with different tokens (very common)
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] Would you like me to show you a clean way to structure this in your `slopfountain` project so you
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] can easily run multiple bot instances with different models?
2026-05-01 13:43:10 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:43:46 [nitro@ryzen5] how do i tell bot is enabled correctly?
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] Here's how to tell if your Discord bot is enabled and running correctly:
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 1. Check in the Discord Developer Portal
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 1. Go to the [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications)
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 2. Open your application
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 3. Click on the Bot tab on the left
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 4. You should see:
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3]    - A green "Online" status (if it's currently running)
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3]    - Your bot's username and avatar
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3]    - The Token section (never share this)
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] If you see "Offline", it just means the bot isn't currently connected — it doesn't mean
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] it's broken.
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 2. Check When You Run the Bot (Most Important)
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] When you start your bot, look for a successful connection message in the console.
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] • Good signs* (examples):
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] // If you're using discord.js
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] client.once('ready', () => {
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3]     console.log(`✅ Bot logged in as ${client.user.tag}`);
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] });
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] // If using raw Discord API / fetch
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] console.log("✅ Connected to Discord Gateway");
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] • Bad signs* (errors you might see):
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] - `Invalid token`
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] - `Disallowed intents`
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] - `Missing Access`
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] - `Privileged intent` errors
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] - `WebSocket connection failed`
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 3. Check Inside Discord
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] After running the bot:
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 1. Go to your Discord server
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 2. Look in the member list (right side)
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 3. Your bot should appear with a green dot (Online)
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 4. It should have the "Bot" tag under its name
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] If the bot is in the server but shows as Offline (gray dot), then it's not connected
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] properly.
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 4. Quick Test
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] The fastest way to verify:
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] - Mention the bot in a channel (`@YourBotName`)
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] - If it responds or shows typing, it's working
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] - Try a simple command if you have one set up
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 5. Common Issues & How to Spot Them
2026-05-01 13:44:05 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] ╭────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] │  Symptom                           │  Likely Problem                           │  How to Fix                               │
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] ├────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] │  Bot doesn't appear in server      │  Not invited or wrong server              │  Re-invite using the OAuth2 URL           │
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] │  Shows as Offline                  │  Bot not running or crashed               │  Check console for errors                 │
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] │  `Invalid Token` error             │  Wrong or expired token                   │  Regenerate token in Developer Portal     │
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] │  `Missing Message Content Intent`  │  Privileged intent not enabled            │  Enable it in the Bot tab                 │
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] │  Bot is online but doesn't reply   │  Missing permissions or intents           │  Check bot permissions in server          │
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] ╰────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] Quick Checklist
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] Run through this when starting a bot:
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] 1. ✅ Correct token loaded from `.env`
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] 2. ✅ Bot shows Online in Developer Portal (after running)
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] 3. ✅ Bot appears in your Discord server with green status
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] 4. ✅ No red errors in the console
2026-05-01 13:44:06 [grok-4.3] 5. ✅ Bot responds to a mention or command
