2026-05-01 13:46:49 [nitro@ryzen5] support server? what is suitable?
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] Here's a clear answer:
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] What is a "Support Server" for Discord Bots?
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] A Support Server is a Discord server where users can go to:
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - Ask questions about the bot
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - Report bugs
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - Get help
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - Give feedback
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - See announcements
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] Discord requires this during verification because they want to make sure there's a real
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] person behind the bot who can actually help users.
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] What is Considered Suitable?
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] Discord is looking for a real, usable support server. Here's what they generally accept:
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] ╭───────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────╮
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] │  Criteria                         │  Suitable                                       │  Not Suitable                               │  Notes                  │
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] ├───────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┤
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] │  **Server exists and is active**  │  Has members and channels                       │  Empty server with no activity              │  They check this        │
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] │  **Has support channels**         │  `#support`, `#help`, `#bugs`, `#feedback`      │  No clear way to ask for help               │  Very important         │
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] │  **You are in the server**        │  You're the owner or have moderator rights      │  You left the server                        │  You must be reachable  │
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] │  **Rules are present**            │  Has basic rules                                │  No rules at all                            │  Shows you're serious   │
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] │  **Bot is in the server**         │  The bot is added and working                   │  Bot is not in the server                   │  Recommended            │
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] │  **Public or private**            │  Can be public or private                       │  Completely hidden                          │  Private is fine        │
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] ╰───────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────╯
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] Recommended Setup (Simple & Effective)
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] For most bots, this structure works well:
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] • Server Name*: Something like `SlopFountain Support` or `Fountain AI Support`
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] • Suggested Channels*:
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - `#welcome` – rules and how to get help
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - `#support` – main channel for questions
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - `#bugs` – report issues
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - `#feedback` – suggestions
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] - `#announcements` – bot updates (read-only for most users)
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] You don't need a huge server. Even a small server with 10–50 members is usually fine as long as it
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] looks functional.
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] How to Add It to Your Application
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 1. Go to your application in the [Discord Developer
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications)
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 2. Go to General Information
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 3. Find the field Support Server
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 4. Paste the invite link to your server
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] Example of a good invite link:
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] https://discord.gg/yourcode
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] Quick Advice for You
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] Since your project is called SlopFountain (an LLM research tool), here are some suitable
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] options:
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:47:03 [grok-4.3] ╭───────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────╮
2026-05-01 13:47:04 [grok-4.3] │  Option                           │  Pros                        │  Cons                       │  Recommendation               │
2026-05-01 13:47:04 [grok-4.3] ├───────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
2026-05-01 13:47:04 [grok-4.3] │  Create a new small server        │  Clean, focused on your bot  │  You have to manage it      │  **Best for now**             │
2026-05-01 13:47:04 [grok-4.3] │  Use an existing personal server  │  Easy                        │  Might look unprofessional  │  Only if it's well organized  │
2026-05-01 13:47:04 [grok-4.3] │  Make the support server public   │  More users can join         │  More moderation work       │  Do this later                │
2026-05-01 13:47:04 [grok-4.3] ╰───────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────╯
