2026-05-01 13:55:42 [nitro@ryzen5] the server lists the application in the discord app but no bot
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] This is a common issue.
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] What's Happening
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] When you see the application listed in the server but no bot, it usually means you
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] added the application (for slash commands / integrations), but you didn't actually invite the
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] bot itself.
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] Discord treats the Application and the Bot as two separate things:
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] - Application = The whole project (shows up in server settings → Integrations)
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] - Bot = The actual user that appears in the member list (this is what you need)
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] How to Fix It
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] You need to invite the bot properly using an OAuth2 link with the `bot` scope.
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] Step-by-step Fix
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 1. Go to the [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications)
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 2. Open your application
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 3. On the left, click OAuth2 → URL Generator
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 4. Under Scopes, check these:
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3]    - `bot`
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3]    - `applications.commands` (if you're using slash commands)
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 5. Under Bot Permissions, select the permissions your bot needs (start with these for
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] testing):
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3]    - `Send Messages`
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3]    - `Read Message History`
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3]    - `Embed Links`
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3]    - `Use Slash Commands`
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 6. Scroll down and copy the generated URL
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 7. Open that link in your browser and select your server
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 8. Click Authorize
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] After doing this, the bot should appear in your server’s member list.
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] Quick Check
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] After inviting with the correct link, go to your server and check:
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] - Does the bot appear in the member list (right side)?
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] - Does it show a green dot (online)?
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:51 [grok-4.3] If it still doesn't show up, let me know what permissions you selected and I’ll help you adjust the
2026-05-01 13:55:52 [grok-4.3] link.
2026-05-01 13:55:52 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 13:55:52 [grok-4.3] Would you like me to give you a recommended permission set for a general-purpose AI bot
2026-05-01 13:55:52 [grok-4.3] like yours?
2026-05-01 13:55:52 [grok-4.3] 
