2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] │  **Tokens & Identity**    │  How will each bot identify itself?                        │  Use different tokens + different bot names (e.g. `SlopFountain` and `SlopFountain-Test`)      │
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] │  **Purpose**              │  What is each bot for?                                     │  Decide early: one for stable use, one for testing/experimentation?                            │
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] │  **Channels**             │  Will they share channels or use separate ones?            │  Strongly recommended to use **different channels** (or different servers) to avoid confusion  │
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] │  **Fountain Connection**  │  Will both bots talk to the same `slopfountain` instance?  │  Possible, but you’ll need to handle message routing carefully                                 │
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] │  **Logging**              │  How will you tell which bot is doing what?                │  Add clear prefixes like `[BOT1]` and `[BOT2]` in logs                                         │
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] │  **Configuration**        │  How will config be managed?                               │  Separate `.env` files or config objects per bot                                               │
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] │  **Deployment**           │  How will you run both at the same time?                   │  PM2, separate terminals, or Deno services                                                     │
