2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] Most people in your situation end up doing one of these two patterns:
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] • Option A: Main + Test Bot (Recommended for now)*
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] - `Bot 1`: Stable / Public-facing bot
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] - `Bot 2`: Testing / Experimental bot (can be more chaotic)
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] - They can both connect to the same fountain, but you route messages based on channel or prefix.
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] 
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] • Option B: Two Independent Personalities*
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] - Two bots with different system prompts / models
2026-05-01 14:04:18 [grok-4.3] - They might even talk to each other in certain channels
